{
  "title": "Dua of Imam Husayn (a.s.) on the Day of Arafah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM. \nIn the Name of Allah, the All-compassionate, the All-merciful.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِیْ لَیْسَ لِقَضَآئِہٖ دَافِعٌ \nALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE LAYSA LEQAZAAA-EHI DAAFE-U’N \nPraise be to Allah Whose determination cannot be repelled by anything,\nوَ لَاْ لِعَطَآئِہٖ مَانِعٌ\nWA LAA LE-A’TAA-EHI MANE-U’N \nWhose gifts cannot be stopped by anything,\nوَ لَاْ كَصُنْعِہٖ صُنْعُ صَانِعٍ \nWA LAA KA-SUN-E’HI SUN-O’ SAANE-I’N \nand Whose making cannot be resembled by the making of anyone.\nوَ هُوَ الْجَوَادُ الْوَاسِعُ \nWA HOWAL JAWAADUL WAA-SE-O’ \nHe is the All-magnanimous, the All-liberal.\nفَطَرَ اَجْنَاسَ الْبَدَائِعِ \nFATARA AJNAASAL BADAA-E-E’ \nHe originated the genus of the wonderfully created things\nوَ اَتْقَنَ بِحِكْمَتِهِ الصَّنَائِعَ \nWA ATQANA BEHIKMATEHIS SANAA-E-A’ \nand He perfected the made things by His wisdom.\nلَاْ تَخْفٰی عَلَیْهِ الطَّلَائِعُ \nLAA TAKHFAA A’LAYHIT TALAA-E-O’ \nAll growing things cannot be hidden from Him\nوَ لَاْ تَضِیْعُ عِنْدَهُ الْوَدَآئِعُ \nWA LAA TAZEE-O’ I’NDAHUL WADAA-E-O’ \nand all things deposited with Him shall never be wasted.\nجَازِیْ كُلِّ صَانِعٍ وَ رَآئِشُ كُلِّ قَانِعٍ \nJAAZEE KULLE SAANE-I’N WA RA-AAA-ESHO KULLE QAANE-I’N \nHe is the Repayer on every deed, the Enricher of every satisfied one,\nوَ رَاحِمُ كُلِّ ضَارِعٍ وَ مُنْزِلُ الْمَنَافِعِ \nWA RAAHEMO KULLE ZAA-RE-I’N WA MUNZELUL MANAA-FE-E’ \nthe Merciful toward every suppliant, and the Revealer of the benefits\nوَ الْكِتَابِ الْجَامِعِ بِالنُّوْرِ السَّاطِعِ \nWAL KETAABIL JAAME-E’ BIN-NOORIS SAATE-E’ \nand the All-comprehensive Book with the glaring light.\nوَ هُوَ لِلدَّعَوَاتِ سَامِعٌ \nWA HOWA LID-DA-A’WAATE SAME-U’N \nHe is also the Hearer of prayers, \nوَ لِلْكُرُبَاتِ دَافِعٌ وَ لِلدَّرَجَاتِ رَافِعٌ\nWA LIL-KOROBAATE DAA-FE-U’N WA LID-DARAJAATE RAAFE-U’N \nthe Warder-off of anguishes, the Raiser of ranks,\nوَ لِلْجَبَابِرَۃِ قَامِعٌ فَلَاْ اِلٰهَ غَیْرُہٗ \nWA LILJABAABERATE QAAME-U’N FALAA ELAAHA GHAYROHU \nand the Suppressor of the tyrants. There is no god other than Him \nوَ لَاْ شَیْءَ یَعْدِلُہٗ \nWA LAA SHAYA YA’DELOHU \nand there is nothing equivalent to Him\nوَ لَیْسَ كَمِثْلِہٖ شَیْءٌ وَ هُوَ السَّمِیْعُ الْبَصِیْرُ \nWA LAYSA KAMISLEHI SHAYUN WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L BASEERUL \nand nothing like a likeness of Him, and He is the All-hearing, the All-seeing, \nاللَّطِیْفُ الْخَبِیْرُ وَ هُوَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nLATEEFUL KHABEERO WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nthe All-gentle, the All-aware, and He has power over all things. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَرْغَبُ اِلَیْكَ وَ اَشْهَدُ بِالرُّبُوْبِیَّۃِ لَكَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ARGHABO ELAYKA WA ASH-HADO BIR-ROBOOBIYYATE LAKA \nO Allah, I willingly desire for You and I testify to the Lordship of You, \nمُقِرًّا بِاَنَّكَ رَبِّیْ \nMOQIRRAN BE-ANNAKA RABBEE \nconfessing that You are verily my Lord\nوَ اَنَّ اِلَیْكَ مَرَدِّیْ اِبْتَدَاتَنِیْ بِنِعْمَتِكَ \nWA ANNA ELAYKA MARADDEE IBTADAA-TANEE BE-NE’MATEKA \nand to You shall be my return. You had begun bestowing on me \nقَبْلَ اَنَ اَكُوْنَ شَیْئًا مَذْكُوْرًا\nQABLA AN AKOONA SHAY-AN MAZKOORAN \nbefore I was anything worth mentioning,\nوَ خَلَقْتَنِیْ مِنَ تُّرَابِ ثُمَّ اَسْكَنْتَنِیْ الْاَصْلَابَ \nWA KHALAQTANEE MENAT TORAABE SUMMA ASKANTANIL ASLAABA \nand You created me from dust. You then put me up in the loins, \nاٰمِنًا لِرَیْبَ الْمَنُوْنَ وَ اخْتِلَافِ الدُّهُوْرِ وَ السِّنِیْنَ \nAAMENAN LERAYBIL MANOONE WAKHTELAAFID DOHOORE WAS SENEENA \n (making me) saved from vicissitudes of time, and change of ages and years. \nفَلَمْ اَزَلْ ظَاعِنًا مِنْ صُلْبٍ اِلٰی رَحْمٍ \nFALAM AZAL ZAA-E’NAN MIN SULBIN ELAA RAHEMIN \nI was moving from a loin to a womb \nفِی تَقَادُمٍ مِّنَ الْاَیَّامِ الْمَاضِیَۃِ\nFEE TAQAADOMIM MENAL AYYAAMIL MAAZEYATE \nthroughout the passage of the past days\nوَ الْقُرُوْنِ الْخَالِیَۃِ \nWAL QOROONIL KHAALEYATE \nand the ancient ages; \nلَمْ تُخْرِجْنِیْ لِرَاْفَتِكَ بِیْ \nLAM TUKHRIJNEE LERAAFATEKA BEE \nas You have not taken me out (to this world) — on account of Your sympathy to me, \nوَ لُطْفِكَ لِیْ وَ اِحْسَانِكَ اِلَیَّ \nWA LUTFEKA LEE WA EHSAANEKA ELAYYA \nand Your kindness to me, and Your compassion to me — \nفِیْ دَوْلَۃِ اَئِمَّۃِ الْكُفْرِ \nFEE DAWLATE AIMMATIL KUFRIL \nin the government of the heads of unbelief \nالَّذِیْنَ نَقَضُوْا عَهْدَكَ وَكَذَّبُوْا رُسُلَكَ \nLAZEENA NAQAZOO A’HDAKA WA KAZZABOO ROSOLAKA \nwho breached their covenant with You and denied Your messengers. \nلٰكِنَّكَ اَخْرَجْتَنِیْ لِلَّذِیْ سَبَقَ لِیْ مِنَ الْهُدٰی\nLAAKINNAKA AKHRAJTANIL LILLAZEE SABAQA LEE MENAL HODAL \nHowever, You took me out on account of the guidance that You have already known about me\nالَّذِیْ لَہٗ یَسَّرْتَنِیْ وَ فِیْهِ اَنْشَاْتَنِیْ \nLAZEE LAHU YASSARTANEE WA FEEHE ANSHAATANEE \nand You have made easy the way to it and You have brought me up in it.\nوَ مِنْ قَبْلِ ذٰلِكَ رَؤُفْتَ‏ بِیْ بِجَمِیْلِ صُنْعِكَ \nWA MIN QABLE RA-UFTA BEE BEJAMEELE SUN-E’KA \nEven before that, You had compassion on me, through Your excellent conferral \nوَ سَوَابِغِ نِعَمِكَ \nWA SAWAABEGHE NE-A’MEKA \nand Your affluent bestowals.\nفَابْتَدَعْتَ خَلْقِیْ مِنْ مَّنِیٍّ یُّمْنٰی \nFABTADA’TA KHALQEE MIN MANIYYIN-Y YUMNAA \nSo, You fashioned my creation from semen that gushed forth \nوَ اَسْكَنْتَنِیْ فِیْ ظُلُمَاتٍ ثَلَاثٍ\nWA ASKANTANEE FEE ZOLOMAATIN SALAASIN \nand put me up in triple darkness\nبَیْنَ لَحْمٍ وَّ دَمٍ وَّ جِلْدٍ لَمْ تُشْهِدْنِیْ خَلْقِیْ \nBAYNA LAHMIN WA DAMINW WA JILDIN LAM TUSH-HIDNEE KHALQEE \namong flesh, blood, and skin. You have not made me witness my creation, \nوَ لَمْ تَجْعَلْ اِلَیَّ شَیْئًا مِّنْ اَمْرِیْ\nWA LAM TAJ-A’L ELAYYA SHAY-AM MIN AMREE \nand You have not referred any part of my creation to me.\nثُمَّ اَخْرَجْتَنِیْ لِلَّذِیْ سَبَقَ لِیْ مِنَ الْهُدٰی\nSUMMA AKHRAJTANEE LIL-LAZEE SABAQA LEE MENAL HODAA \nYou then took me out on account of the guidance that You have already known about me\nاِلَی الدُّنْیَا تَآمًّا سَوِیًّا \nELAD DUNYAA TAAAM-MAN SAWIYYAN \nto the world, perfect and in sound health. \nوَ حَفِظْتَنِیْ فِی الْمَهْدِ طِفْلًا صَبِیًّا\nWA HAFIZTANEE FIL MAHDE TIFLAN SABIYYAN \nYou have safeguarded me in the cradle\nوَ رَزَقْتَنِیْ مِنَ الْغِذَآءِ لَبَنًا مَرِیًّا \nWA RAZAQTANEE MENAL GHEZAAA-E LABANAN MARIYYAN \nas small child. You have provided me with wholesome milk as food. \nوَ عَطَفْتَ عَلَیَّ قُلُوْبَ الْحَوَاضِنِ\nWA A’TAFTA A’LAYYA QOLOOBAL HAWAAZENE \nYou have made the hearts of the nursemaids tender.\nوَ كَفَّلْتَنِيْ الْاُمَّهَاتِ الرَّوَاحِمَ \nWA KAFFALTANIL UMMAHAATIR RAWAAHEMA \nYou have given me into the charge of merciful mothers. \nوَ كَلَأْتَنِیْ مِنْ طَوَارِقِ الْجَآنِّ \nWA KALAATANEE MIN TAWAAREQIL JAAAN-NE \nYou have saved me from the visits of the Jinn. \nوَ سَلَّمْتَنِیْ مِنَ الزِّیَادَۃِ وَ النُّقْصَانِ \nWA SALLAMTANEE MENAZ ZEYAADATE WAN NUQSAANE \nAnd You have delivered me from increase and decrease. \nفَتَعَالَیْتَ یَا رَحِیْمُ یَا رَحْمٰنُ\nFA-TA-A’ALAYTA YAA RAHEEMO YAA RAHMAANO \nSo, Exalted be You, O All-merciful, \nحَتّٰی اِذَا اسْتَهْلَلْتُ نَاطِقًا بِالْكَلَامِ \nHATTAA EZAS TAHLALTO NAATEQAN BIL-KALAAME \nO All-beneficent. When I commenced (my life) by pronouncing words, \nاَتْمَمْتَ عَلَیَّ سَوَابِغَ الْاِنْعَامِ \nATMAMTA A’LAYYA SAWAABEGHAL IN-A’AME \nYou perfected for me the affluent bestowals, \nوَ رَبَّیْتَنِیْ زَایِدًا فِیْ كُلِّ عَامٍ \nWA RABBAYTANEE ZAAYEDAN FEE KULLE A’AMIN \nand brought me up with an increase every year. \nحَتّٰی اِذَا اكْتَمَلَتْ فِطْرَتِیْ \nHATTAA EZAK TAMALAT FITRATEE \nWhen my creation was accomplished, \nوَ اعْتَدَلَتْ مِرَّتِیْ اَوْجَبْتَ عَلَیَّ حُجَّتَكَ \nWA’ TADALAT MIRRATEE AWJABTA A’LAYYA HUJJATAKA \nand my power became straight, You put me under the obligation of Your Claim,\nبِاَنْ اَلْهَمْتَنِیْ مَعْرِفَتَكَ \nBE-AN ALHAMTANEE MA’REFATAKA \nwhich is that You inspired me with recognition of You \nوَ رَوَّعْتَنِیْ بِعَجَآئِبِ حِكْمَتِكَ \nWA RAWWA’TANEE BE-A’JAAYEBE HIKMATEKA \nand alarmed me by the wonders of Your wisdom,\nوَ اَیْقَظْتَنِیْ لِمَا ذَرَأْتَ فِیْ سَمَآئِكَ وَ اَرْضِكَ \nWA AYQAZTANEE LEMAA ZARAATA FEE SAMAAA-EKA WA ARZEKA \nand You aroused in me that which You created in Your heavens and lands, \nمِنْۢ بَدَآئِعِ خَلْقِكَ\nMIM BADAA-E-E’ KHALQEKA \nwhich is the excellent creation of You.\nوَ نَبَّهْتَنِیْ لِشُكْرِكَ وَ ذِكْرِكَ \nWA NABBAHTANEE LESHUKREKA WA ZIKREKA \nYou attracted my attentions to thank and mention You. \nوَ اَوْجَبْتَ عَلَیَّ طَاعَتَكَ وَ عِبَادَتَكَ \nWA AWJABTA A’LAYYA TAA-A’TAKA WA E’BAADATAKA \nYou made obligatory on me to obey and worship You. \nوَ فَهَمْتَنِیْ مَا جَآئَتْ بِہٖ رُسُلُكَ \nWA FAHHAMTANEE MAA JAA-AT BEHI ROSOLOKA \nYou made me understand that with which Your Apostles came.\nوَ یَسَّرْتَ لِیْ تَقَبُّلَ مَرْضَاتِكَ \nWA YASSARTA LEE TAQABBOLA MARZAATEKA \nYou made easy for me to find agreeable Your pleasure. \nوَ مَنَنْتَ عَلَیَّ فِیْ جَمِیْعِ ذٰلِكَ \nWA MANANTA A’LAYYA FEE JAMEE-E’ ZAALEKA \nYou bestowed upon me with the favor of all that,\nبِعَوْنِكَ وَ لُطْفِكَ ثُمَّ اِذْ خَلَقْتَنِیْ مِنْ خَیْرِ الثَّرٰی \nBE-A’WNEKA WA LUTFEKA SUMMA IZ KHALAQTANEE MIN KHAYRIS SARAA \nout of Your aid and Your gentleness. As You created me from the best of soil, \nلَمْ تَرْضَ لِیْ یَا اِلٰهِیْ نِعْمَۃً دُوْنَ اُخْرٰی \nLAM TARZA LEE YAA ELAAHI NE’MATAN DOONA UKHRAA \nYou, my God, have not wanted for me to have a certain favor (and to be deprived of another) \nوَ رَزَقْتَنِیْ مِنْ اَنْوَاعِ الْمَعَاشِ\nWA RAZAQTANEE MIN ANWAA-I’L MA-A’ASHE \nand You therefore provided me with the various kinds of living\nوَصُنُوْفِ الرِّیَاشِ بِمَنِّكَ الْعَظِیْمِ الْاَعْظَمِ عَلَیَّ \nWA SONOOFIR REYAASHE BEMANNEKAL A’ZEEMIL A-A’ZAME A’LAYYA \nand types of wealth, out of Your great and grand conferral upon me,\nوَ اِحْسَانِكَ الْقَدِیْمِ اِلَیَّ حَتّٰی اِذَا اَتْمَمْتَ عَلَیَّ جَمِیْعَ النِّعَمِ \nWA EHSAANEKAL QADEEME ELAYYA HATTAA EZAA ATMAMTA A’LAYYA JAMEE-A’N NE-A’ME \nand Your eternal kindness to me. As You perfected for me all the graces \nوَ صَرَفْتَ عَنِّیْ كُلَّ النِّقَمِ لَمْ یَمْنَعْكَ جَهْلِیْ وَ جُرْاَتِیْ عَلَیْكَ \nWA SARAFTA A’NNEE KULLAN NEQAME LAM YAMNA’KA JAHLEE WA JUR-ATEE A’LAYKA \nand warded off all misfortunes, my ignorance of You and challenge have not stopped You\nاَنْ دَلَلْتَنِیْ اِلٰی مَا یُقَرِّبُنِیْ اِلَیْكَ \nAN DALALTANEE ELAA MAA YOQARREBONEE ELAYKA \nfrom showing me that which takes me near to You, \nوَ وَفَّقْتَنِیْ لِمَا یُزْلِفُنِیْ لَدَیْكَ \nWA WAFFAQTANEE LEMAA YUZLEFONEE LADAYKA \nand from leading me to that which grants me proximity to You. \nفَاِنْ دَعَوْتُكَ اَجَبْتَنِیْ وَ اِنْ سَئَلْتُكَ اَعْطَیْتَنِیْ \nFA-IN DA-A’WTOKA AJABTANEE WA IN SA-ALTOKA A-A’TAYTANEE \nSo, if I pray You, You will respond to me; and if I beg You, You will give me; \nوَ اِنْ اَطَعْتُكَ شَكَرْتَنِیْ وَ اِنْ شَكَرْتُكَ زِدْتَنِیْ \nWA IN ATA’TOKA SHAKARTANEE WA IN SHAKARTOKA ZID-TANEE \nand if I obey You, You will thank me; and if I thank You, You will give me more. \nكُلُّ ذٰلِكَ اِكْمَالًا لِاَنْعُمِكَ عَلَیَّ \nKULLO ZAALEKA IKMAALAN LE-AN-O’MEKA A’LAYYA \nAll that is completion of Your favors for me, \nوَ اِحْسَانِكَ اِلَیَّ فَسُبْحَانَكَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nWA EHSAANEKA ELAYYA FA-SUBHAANAKA SUBHAANAKA \nand Your kindness to me. So, all glory be to You; all glory be to You.\nمِنْۢ مُبْدِئٍ مُعِیْدٍ \nMIM MUBDE-IN MO-E’EDIN \nYou are verily Originator and Reproducer (of the creation) and \nحَمِیْدٍ مَّجِیْدٍ \nHAMEEDIM MAJEEDIN \nworthy of all praise and full of all glory. \nتَقَدَّسَتْ اَسْمَآؤُكَ وَ عَظُمَتْ اٰلَآؤُكَ\nTAQADDASAT ASMAAA-OKA WA A’ZOMAT AAALAA-OKA \nHoly be Your Names as Your bounties are so immeasurable.\nفَاَیُّ نِعَمِكَ یَا اِلٰهِیْ اُحْصِیْ عَدَدًا وَّ ذِكْرًا \nFA-AYYO NE-A’MEKA YAA ELAAHEE OHSEE A’DADANW WA ZIKRAN \nWhich of Your favors, O my God, can I count in numbers and examples?\nاَمْ اَیُّ عَطَایَاكَ اَقُوْمُ بِهَا شُكْرًا \nAM AYYO A’TAAYAAKA AQOOMO BEHAA SHUKRAN \nOr which of Your gifts can I thank properly? \nوَ هِیَ یَا رَبِّ اَكْثَرُ مِنْ اَنْ یُّحْصِیَهَا الْعَآدُّوْنَ\nWA HEYA YAA RABBE AKSARO MIN AN-Y YOHSEYAHAL A’AAD-DOONA \nThey are, O my Lord, too numerous to be counted by counters\nاَوْیَبْلُغَ عِلْمًا بِهَا الْحَافِظُوْنَ\nAW YABLOGHA I’LMAN BEHAL HAAFEZOONA \nor to be realized by memorizers.\nثُمَّ مَا صَرَفْتَ وَ دَرَأْتَ عَنِّیْ \nSUMMA MAA SARAFTA WA DARAATA A’NNEE \nMoreover, that which You have warded off and repelled, \nاَللّٰهُمَّ مِنَ الضُّرِّ وَ الضَّرَّآءِ\nALLAAHUMMA MENAZ ZURRE WAZ ZARRAA-E \nO Allah, from (the various kinds of) harm and mischief\nاَكْثَرَ مِمَّا ظَهَرَ لِیْ مِنَ الْعَافِیَۃِ وَ السَّرَّآءِ \nAKSARA MIMMAA ZAHARA LEE MENAL A’AFEYATE WAS SARRAAA-E \nis more than that which came to me from wellbeing and joy.\nوَ اَنَا اَشْهَدُ یَا اِلٰهِیْ بِحَقِیْقَۃِ اِیْمَانِیْ \nWA ANAA ASH-HADO YAA ELAAHEE BEHAQEEQATE EEMAANEE \nAnd I bear witness, O my God, with my true belief, \nوَ عَقْدِ عَزَمَاتِ یَقِیْنِیْ \nWA A’QDE A’ZAMAATE YAQEENEE \nand the fortitude of the determinations of my conviction\nوَ خَالِصِ صَرِیْحِ تَوْحِیْدِیْ \nWA KHAALESE SAREEHE TAWHEEDEE \nand the purity of my open belief in Your Oneness \nوَ بَاطِنِ مَكْنُوْنِ ضَمِیْرِیْ \nWA BAATENE MAKNOONE ZAMEEREE \nand the essence of the secret of my conscience,\nوَ عَلَآئِقِ مَجَارِیْ نُوْرِ بَصَرِیْ \nWA A’LAA-EQE MAJAAREE NOORE BASAREE \nand the ties of the canals of the light of my sight, \nوَ اَسَارِیْرِ صَفْحَۃِ جَبِیْنِیْ \nWA ASAA-REERE SAFHATE JABEENEE \nand the lines of my forehead\nوَ خُرْقِ مَسَارِبِ نَفْسِیْ \nWA KHURQE MASAAREBE NAFSEE \nand the hallows of the courses of my breath, \nوَ خَذَارِیْفِ مَارِنِ عِرْنِیْنِیْ \nWA KHAZAAREEFE MAARENE I’RNEENEE \nand the (nasal) cavities of my nose,\nوَ مَسَارِبِ سِمَاخِ سَمْعِیْ \nWA MASAAREBE SEMAA-KHE SAM-E’E \nand the courses of the meatus of my hearing,\nوَ مَا ضُمَّتْ وَ اَطْبَقَتْ عَلَیْهِ شَفَتَایَ \nWA MAA ZUMMAT WA ATBAQAT A’LAYHE SHAFATAAYA \nand whatever my two lips hide and cover up,\nوَ حَرَكَاتِ لَفْظِ لِسَانِیْ \nWA HARAKAATE LAFZE LESAANEE \nand the motions of the vocalization of my tongue,\nوَ مَغْرَزِ حَنَكِ فَمِیْ وَ فَكِّیْ\nWA MAGHRAZE HANAKE FAMEE WA FAKKEE \nand the socket of the palate of my mouth and jaw,\nوَ مَنَابِتِ اَضْرَاسِیْ \nWA MANAABETE AZRAASEE \nand the matrices of my dents,\nوَ مَسَاغِ مَطْعَمِیْ وَ مَشْرَبِی \nWA MASAAGHE MAT-A’MEE WA MASHRABEE \nand the tasting of my food and my drink, \nوَ حِمَالَۃِ اُمِّ رَاسِیْ\nWA HEMAALATE UMME RAASEE \nand the carrier of my skill,\nوَ بُلُوْعِ فَارِغِ حَبَائِلِ عُنُقِیْ \nWA BOLOOGHE FAAREGHE HABAA-ELE O’NOQEE \nand the tube of the tissues of my neck\nوَ مَا اشْتَمَلَ عَلَیْهِ تَامُوْرُ صَدْرِیْ \nWA MASH TAMALA A’LAYHE TAAMOORO SADREE \nand what is included by the cloak of my chest,\nوَ حَمَایِلِ حَبْلِ وَ تِیْنِیْ وَ نِیَاطِ حِجَابِ قَلْبِیْ \nWA HAMAA-YELE HABLE WATEENEE WA NEYAATE HEJAABE QALBEE \nand the carriers of the cord of my aorta, and the cords of the pericardium of my heart,\nوَ اَفْلَاذِ حَوَاشِیْ كَبِدِیْ \nWA AFLAAZE HAWAASHEE KABEDEE \nand the pieces of the retinues of my liver,\nوَ مَا حَوَتْهُ شَرَاسِیْفُ اَضْلَاعِیْ \nWA MAA HAWAT-HO SHARAASEEFO AZLAAE’E \nand that which is included by the cartilages of my ribs,\nوَ حِقَاقُ مَفَاصِلِیْ وَ قَبْضُ عَوَامِلِیْ \nWA HEQAAQO MAFAASELEE WA QABZO AWAAMELEE \nand the cavities of my joints, and the interactings of my organisms,\nوَ اَطْرَافُ اَنَامِلِیْ وَ لَحْمِیْ وَ دَمِیْ \nWA ATRAAFO ANAAMELEE WA LAHMEE WA DAMEE \nand the extremes of my fingertips, and my flesh, and my blood,\nوَ شَعْرِیْ وَ بَشَرِیْ وَ عَصَبِیْ وَ قَصَبِیْ \nWA SHA’REE WA BASHAREE WA A’SABEE WA QASABEE \nand my hair, and my skin, and my nerve, and my sinews,\nوَ عِظَامِیْ وَ مُخِّیْ وَ عُرُوْقِیْ وَ جَمِیْعِ جِوَارِحِیْ \nWA E’ZAAMEE WA MUKHKHI WA O’ROOQEE WA JAMEE-E’ JAWAAREHEE \nand my bones, and my brain, and my veins, and all of my organs,\nوَ مَا انْتَسَجَ عَلٰی ذٰلِكَ اَیَّامَ رِضَاعِیْ \nWA MAN TASAJA A’LAA ZAALEKA AYYAAMA REZAA-E’E \nand that which was pieced together during the days of my suckling,\nوَ مَا اَقَلَّتِ الْاَرْضُ مِنِّیْ \nWA MAA AQALLATIL ARZO MINNEE \nand whatever of my body that the ground carries,\nوَ نَوْمِیْ وَ یَقْظَتِیْ وَ سُكُوْنِیْ \nWA NAWMEE WA YAQAZATEE WA SOKOONEE \nand my sleeping, and my wakefulness, and my motionlessness,\nوَ حَرَكَاتِ رُكُوْعِیْ وَ سُجُوْدِیْ \nWA HARAKAATE ROKOO-E’E WA SOJOODEE \nand the movements of my bowing and prostration;\nاَنْ لَوْ حَاوَلْتُ وَ اجْتَهَدْتُ مَدَی الْاَعْصَارِ \nAN LAW HAAWALTO WAJ TAHADTO MADAL A-A’SAARE \n (by all that I bear witness) that if I try my best and strive throughout all ages\nوَ الْاَحْقَابِ لَوْ عُمِّرْتُهَا \nWAL AHQAABE LAW U’MMIRTOHAA \nand all times, if I live them,\nاَنْ اُؤَدِّیَ شُكْرَ وَاحِدَۃٍ مِنْ اَنْعُمِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ ذٰلِكَ \nAN O-ADDEYA SHUKRA WAAHEDATIN MIN AN-O’MEKA MAS TATA’TO ZAALEKA \nto thank properly only one of Your favors, I will not be able to do that,\nاِلَّا بِمَنِّكَ الْمُوْجِبِ عَلَیَّ بِہٖ شُكْرَكَ \nILLAA BEMANNEKAL MOOJEBE A’LAYYA BEHI SHUKRAKA \nexcept through a favor of You, which also requires me to thank You for it,\nاَبَدًا جَدِیْدًا وَ ثَنَآءً طَارِفًا عَتِیْدًا \nABADAN JADEEDAN WA SANAAA-AN TAAREFAN A’TEEDAN \nonce again with new thanking and with praise that is newly acquired and newly prepared.\nاَجَلْ وَ لَوْ حَرَصْتُ اَنَا وَ الْعَآدُّوْنَ مِنْ اَنَامِكَ \nAJAL WA LAW HARASTO ANAA WAL A’AAD-DOONA MIN ANAAMEKA \nTrue is this! And if I try hard, as well as the counters from Your creatures,\nاَنْ نُحْصِیَ مَدٰی اِنْعَامِكَ سَالِفِہٖ وَ اٰنِفِہٖ \nAN NOHSEYA MADAA IN-A’AMEKA SAALEFEHI WA AANEFEHI \nto count the scope of Your favoring, both the past and the present,\nمَا حَصَرْنَاهُ عَدَدًا وَ لَاْ اَحْصَیْنَاهُ اَمَدًا \nMAA HASARNAAHO A’DADAN WA LAA AHSAYNAAHO AMADAN \nwe shall never be able to calculate it in number, or count it in time.\nهَیْهَاتَ اَنّٰی ذٰلِكَ \nHAY-HAATA ANNAA ZAALEKA \nToo far is this! How can it be!\nوَ اَنْتَ الْمُخْبِرُ  فِیْ كِتَابِكَ النَّاطِقِ \nWA ANTAL MUKHBERO FEE KETAABEKAN NAATEQE \nWhile it is You Who have informed in Your rational Book\nوَ النَّبَاِ الصَّادِقِ \nWAN NABA-IS SAADEQE \nand true news:\nوَ اِنْ تَعُدُّوْا نِعْمَۃَ اﷲِ لَاْ تُحْصُوْهَا \nWA IN TA-U’DDOO NE’MATAL LAAHE LAA TOHSOOHAA \n “And if you count Allah's favors, you will not be able to number them.”\nصَدَقَ كِتَابُكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اِنْۢبَآؤُكَ \nSADAQA KETAABOKA ALLAAHUMMA WA IMBAAA-OKA \nTrue is Your Book, O Allah, and Your informing.\nوَ بَلَّغَتْ اَنْبِیَآؤُكَ وَ رُسُلُكَ \nWA BALLAGHAT AMBEYAAA-OKA WA ROSOLOKA \nYour Prophets and Messengers have conveyed\nمَا اَنْزَلْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ وَحْیِكَ \nMAA ANZALTA A’LAYHIM MIN WAHYEKA \nwhat You revealed to them, from Your Revelation,\nوَ شَرَعْتَ لَهُمْ وَ بِهِمْ مِنْ دِیْنِكَ \nWA SHARA’TA LAHUM WA BEHIM MIN DEENEKA \nand what You have made plain for them and through them Your religion.\nغَیْرَ اَنِّیْ یَا اِلٰهِیْ \nGHAYRA ANNEE YAA ELAAHEE \nNevertheless, O my God,\nاَشْهَدُ بِجُهْدِیْ وَ جِدِّیْ \nASH-HADO BEJOHDEE WA JIDDEE \nI bear witness by my ultimate possibility and my diligence\nوَ مَبْلَغِ طَاعَتِیْ وَ وُسْعِیْ وَ اَقُوْلُ مُؤْمِنًا مُوْقِیًا \nWA MABLAGHE TAA-A’TEE WA WUS-E’E WA AQOOLO MOA-MENAN MOOQENAN \nand the scope of my vigor and my capacity, and I say with full faith and conviction:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِیْ لَمْ یَتَّخِذْ وَ لَدًا فَیَكُوْنَ مَوْرُوْثًا \nALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE LAM YATTAKHIZ WALADAN FAYAKOONO MAWROOSAN \nAll praise be to Allah Who has not taken to Himself a son to be inherited,\nوَ لَمْ یَكُنْ لَّہٗ شَرِیْكٌ فِیْ مُلْكِہٖ \nWA LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FEE MULKEHI \nand Who does not have a partner in His kingdom,\nفَیُضَآدُّہٗ فِیْمَا ابْتَدَعَ \nFAYOZAADDOHU FEEMAB TADA-A’ \nto oppose Him in what He fashions,\nوَ لَا وَ لِیٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ \nWA LAA WALIYYUM MENAZ ZULLE \nand Who does not have a helper to save Him from disgrace,\nفَیُرْفِدَہٗ فِیْمَا صَنَعَ فَسُبْحَانَہٗ سُبْحَانَہٗ \nFAYURFEDAHU FEEMAA SANA-A’ FASUBHAANAHU SUBHAANAHU \nto help Him in what He makes. So, glory be to Him, glory be to Him.\nلَوْ كَانَ فِیْهِمَا اٰلِهَۃٌ اِلَّا اﷲُ \nLAW KAANA FEEHEMAA AALEHATUN ILLAL LAAHO \nIf there had been in them any gods except Allah, they would both have \nلَفَسَدَتَا وَ تَفَطَّرَتَا \nLAFASADATAA WA TAFATTARATAA \ncertainly been in a state of disorder and destruction.\nسُبْحَانَ اﷲِ الْوَاحِدِ الْاَحَدِ الصَّمَدِ \nSUBHAANAL LAAHIL WAAHEDIL AHADIS SAMADIL \nAll glory be to Allah, the One, the Only One, the Besought of all,\nالَّذِیْ لَمْ یَلِدْ وَ لَمْ یُوْلَدْ وَ لَمْ یَكُنْ لَّہٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ \nLAZEE LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUL LAHU KOFOWAN AHADUN \nWho begets not nor is He begotten, and there is none like Him.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ حَمْدًا یُعَادِلُ حَمْدَ مَلَآئِكَتِهِ الْمُقَرَّبِیْنَ \nALHAMDO LILLAAHE HAMDAN YO-A’ADELO HAMDA MALAAA-EKATEHIL MOQARRABEENA \nAll praise be to Allah — praise that is equal to the praise of His Favorite Angels,\nوَ اَنْۢبِیَآئِهِ الْمُرْسَلِیْنَ وَ صَلَّی اﷲُ عَلٰی خِیَرَتِہٖ \nWA AMBEYAAA-EHIL MURSALEENA WA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAA KHEYARATEHI \nand His missioned Prophets. May Allah send blessings to His Select,\nمُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَّمِ النَّبِیِّیْنَ \nMOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA \nMuhammad, the Seal of Prophets,\nوَ اٰلِهِ الطَّیِّبِیْنَ الطَّاهِرِیْنَ \nWA AALEHIT TAYYEBEENAT TAAHEREENAL \nand upon his Household, the pure, immaculate, \nالْمُخْلَصِیْنَ وَ سَلَّمَ \nMUKHLASEENA WA SALLAM.\nand well-chosen, and may He send benedictions upon them.\nImam (a.s.) then besought Almighty Allah so earnestly that his eyes shed tears. He then said:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِیْ اَخْشَاكَ كَاَنِّیْ اَرَاكَ \nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNEE AKHSAAKA KA-ANNEE ARAAKA \nO Allah, (please) make me fear You as if I can see You.\nوَ اَسْعِدْنِیْ بِتَقْوٰیكَ وَ لَاْ تُشْقِنِیْ بِمَعْصِیَتِكَ \nWA AS-I’DNEE BETAQWAAKA WA LAA TUSHQENEE BEMA’SEYATEKA \nMake happy by fearing You. Do not make me unhappy by disobeying You.\nوَ خِرْ لِیْ فِیْ قَضَآئِكَ وَ بَارِكْ لِیْ فِیْ قَدَرِكَ \nWA KHIR LEE FEE QAZAAA-EKA WA BAARIK LEE FEE QADAREKA \nChoose for me through Your decree. Bless me through Your determination,\nحَتّٰی لَاْ اُحِبَّ تَعْجِیْلَ مَا اَخَّرْتَ \nHATTAA LAA OHIBBA TA’JEELA MAA AKHKHARTA \nso that I will not long for hastening that which You have delayed\nوَ لَاْ تَاْخِیْرَ مَا عَجَّلْتَ \nWA LAA TAAKHEERA MAA A’JJALTA \nor delaying that which You would hasten.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ غِنَایَ فِیْ نَفْسِیْ \nALLAAHUMMAJ A’L GHENAAYA FEE NAFSEE \nO Allah, (please) make my richness in my conscience,\nوَ الْیَقِیْنَ فِیْ قَلْبِیْ وَ الْاِخْلَاصَ فِیْ عَمْلِیْ \nWAL YAQEENA FEE QALBEE WAL IKHLAASA FEE A’MALEE \nconviction in my heart, sincerity in my deeds,\nوَ النُّوْرَ فِی بَصَرِیْ وَ الْبَصِیْرَۃَ فِیْ دِیْنِیْ \nWAN NOORA FEE BASAREE WAL-BASEERATA FEE DEENEE \nlight in my sight, and insight in my religion.\nوَ مَتِّعْنِیْ بِجَوَارِحِیْ \nWA MATTE’NEE BEJAWAAREHEE \nMake me find enjoyment in my organs.\nوَ اجْعَلْ سَمْعِیْ وَ بَصَرِیَ الْوَارِثَیْنِ مِنِّیْ \nWAJ A’L SAM-E’E WA BASAREYAL WAARESAINE MINNEE \nMake my hearing and my sight sound until I am inherited.\nوَ انْصُرْنِیْ عَلٰی مَنْ ظَلَمَنِیْ \nWAN SURNEE A’LAA MAN ZALAMANEE \nGrant me victory over him who wrongs me,\nوَ اَرِنِیْ فِیْهِ ثَأْرِیْ وَ مَأْرِبِیْ \nWA ARENEE FEEHE SAAREE WA MAA-REBEE \nmake me witness my avenge and objective in him,\nوَ اَقِرَّ بِذٰلِكَ عَیْنِیْ \nWA AQIRRA BEZAALEKA A’YNEE \nand make it the delight of my eye. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اكْشِفْ كُرْبَتِیْ \nALLAAHUMMAK SHIF KURBATEE \nO Allah, (please) relieve my agony,\nوَاسْتُرْ عَوْرَتِیْ وَاغْفِرْلِیْ خَطِٓیْئَتِیْ \nWAS TUR A’WRATEE WAGH FIR LEE KHATEE-ATEE \nconceal my flaws, forgive my sin,\nوَ اخْسَاْ شَیْطَانِیْ وَ فُكَ رِهَانِیْ \nWAKH SAA SHAYTAANEE WA FUKKA REHAANEE \ndrive away my devil from me, redeem my mortgage,\nوَ اجْعَلْ لِیْ یَا اِلٰهِی الدَّرَجَۃَ الْعُلْیَا فِی الْاٰخِرَۃِ وَ الْاُوْلٰی \nWAJ A’L LEE YAA ELAAHID DARAJATAL U’LYAA FIL AAKHERATE WAL OOLAA \nand decide for me, O my God, the supreme rank in the Hereafter and in the former (life).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ كَمَا خَلَقْتَنِیْ \nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HAMDO KAMAA KHALAQTANEE \nO Allah, all praise be to You for You have created me\nفَجَعَلْتَنِیْ سَمِیْعًاۢ بَصِیْرًا \nFA-JA-A’LTANEE SAMEE-A’M BASEERAN \nand made me hear and see. \nوَ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ كَمَا خَلَقْتَنِیْ \nWA LAKAL HAMDO KAMAA KHALAQTANEE \nAll praise be to You for you have created me\nفَجَعَلْتَنِیْ خَلْقًا سَوِیًّا رَحْمَۃً بِیْ \nFA-JA-A’LTANEE KHALQAN SAWIYYAN RAHMATAN BEE \nand made my creation perfect, on account of Your having mercy on me,\nوَ قَدْ كُنْتَ عَنْ خَلْقِیْ غَنِیًّا \nWA QAD KUNTA A’N KHALQEE GHANIYYAN \nand You could dispense with creating me.\nرَبِّ بِمَا بَرَأْتَنِیْ فَعَدَّلْتَ فِطْرَتِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA BARAATANEE FA-A’DDALTA FITRATEE \nO my Lord, as You gave rise to me and perfected my creation;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَنْشَاْتَنِیْ فَاَحْسَنْتَ صُوْرَتِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA ANSHAATANEE FA-AHSANTA SOORATEE \nO my Lord, as You originated me and did well my form;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَحْسَنْتَ اِلَیَّ وَ فِیْ نَفْسِیْ عَافَیْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA AHSANTA ELAYYA WA FEE NAFSEE A’AFAYTANEE \nO my Lord, as You conferred favors on me and granted me wellbeing in myself;\nرَبِّ بِمَا كَلَاْ تَنِیْ وَ وَفَّقْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA KALAATANEE WA WAFFAQTANEE \nO my Lord, as You saved me and led me to success;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَیَّ فَهَدَیْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA AN-A’MTA A’LAYYA FAHADAYTANEE \nO my Lord, as You bestowed favors on me and guided me;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَوْلَیْتَنِیْ وَ مِنْ كُلِّ خَیْرٍ اَعْطَیْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA AWLAYTANEE WA MIN KULLE KHAYRIN A-A’TAYTANEE \nO my Lord, as You presented me and gave me from every good;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَطْعَمْتَنِیْ وَ سَقَیْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA A-TA’MTANEE WA SAQAYTANEE \nO my Lord, as you fed me and watered me;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَغْنَیْتَنِیْ وَ اَقْنَیْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA AGHNAYTANEE WA AQNAYTANEE \nO my Lord, as You enriched me and gave me to hold;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَعَنْتَنِیْ وَ اَعْزَزْتَنِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA A-A’NTANEE WA A-A’ZAZTANEE \nO my Lord, as You helped me and braced me;\nرَبِّ بِمَا اَلْبَسْتَنِیْ مِنْ سِتْرِكَ الصَّافِیْ \nRABBE BEMAA ALBASTANEE MIN SITREKAS SAAFEE \nO my Lord, as you clothed me from Your pure cover\nوَ یَسَّرْتَ لِیْ مِنْ صُنْعِكَ الْكَافِیْ \nWA YASSARTA LEE MIN SUN-E’KAL KAAFEE \nand made easy for me Your adequate making,\nصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nso, (please) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَ اَعِنِّیْ عَلٰی بَوَآئِقِ الدُّهُوْرِ \nWA A-I’NNEE A’LAA BAWAA-EQID DOHOORE \nhelp me against calamities of ages \nوَ صُرُوْفِ اللَّیَالِیْ وَ الْاَیَّامِ \nWA SOROOFIL LAYAALEE WAL AYYAAME \nand changes of nights and days,\nوَ نَجِّنِیْ مِنْ اَهْوَالِ الدُّنْیَا وَ كُرُبَاتِ الْاٰخِرَۃِ \nWA NAJJENEE MIN AHWAALID DUNYAA WA KOROBAATIL AAKHERATE \nrescue me from the horrors of this world and the anguishes of the Hereafter,\nوَاكْفِنِیْ شَرَّ مَا یَعْمَلُ الظَّالِمُوْنَ فِی الْاَرْضِ \nWAK FENEE SHARRA MAA YA’MALUZ ZAALEMOONA FIL ARZE \nand save me from the evils of what the wrongdoers do in the earth.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَا اَخَافُ فَاكْفِنِیْ \nALLAAHUMMA MAA AKHAAFO FAKFENEE \nO Allah, as to what I anticipate, (please) save me (from it).\nوَ مَا اَحْذَرُ فَقِنِیْ \nWA MAA AHZARO FAQENEE \nAs to what I watch out, (please) protect me (against it).\nوَ فِیْ نَفْسِیْ وَ دِیْنِیْ فَاحْرُسْنِیْ وَ فِیْ سَفَرِیْ فَاحْفَظْنِیْ \nWA FEE NAFSEE WA DEENEE FAHRUSNEE WA FEE SAFAREE FAHFAZNEE \nSafeguard me in my soul and religion, watch over me in my journeys,\nوَ فِیْ اَهْلِیْ وَ مَالِیْ فَاخْلُفْنِیْ \nWA FEE AHLEE WA MAALEE FAKHLUFNEE \nbe in charge of my family members and properties during my absence,\nوَ فِیْ مَا رَزَقْتَنِیْ فَبَارِكْ لِیْ \nWA FEE MAA RAZAQTANEE FABAARIK LEE \nbless me in that which You provide as sustenance,\nوَ فِیْ نَفْسِیْ فَذَلِّلْنِیْ وَ فِیْ اَعْیُنِ النَّاسِ فَعَظِّمْنِیْ \nWA FEE NAFSEE FA-ZALLILNEE WA FEE A-A’YONIN NAASE FA-A’ZZIMNEE \nmake me see myself as humble, make people see me as great,\nوَ مِنْ شَرِّ الْجِنِّ وَ الْاِنْسِ فَسَلِّمْنِیْ \nWA MIN SHARRIL JINNE WAL INSE FASALLIMNEE \nkeep me sound from the evils of the Jinn and people,\nوَ بِذُنُوْبِیْ فَلَاْ تَفْضَحْنِیْ \nWA BE-ZONOOBEE FALAA TAFZAHNEE \ndo not disclose me because of my sins,\nوَ بِسَرِیْرَتِیْ فَلَاْ تُخْزِنِیْ \nWA BESAREERATEE FALAA TUKHZENEE \ndo not disgrace me because of the secret side (of myself),\nوَ بِعَمَلِیْ فَلَاْ تَبْتَلِنِیْ \nWA BEA’MALEE FALAA TABTALENEE \ndo not try me in my deeds, \nوَ نِعَمَكَ فَلَاْ تَسْلُبْنِیْ \nWA NE-A’MAKA FALAA TASLUBNEE \ndo not deprive me of Your bounties,\nوَ اِلٰی غَیْرِكَ فَلَاْ تَكِلْنِیْ \nWA ELAA GHAYREKA FALAA TAKILNEE \nand do not refer me to anyone other than You.\nاِلٰهِیْ اِلٰی مَنْ تَكِلُنِیْ \nELAAHEE ELAA MAN TAKELONEE \nTo whom do You entrust me?\nاِلٰی قَرِیْبٍ فَیَقْطَعُنِیْ \nELAA QAREEBIN FAYAQTA-O’NEE \nTo a relative, and he will rupture my relation with him!\nاَمْ اِلٰی بَعِیْدٍ فَیَتَجَهَمُنِیْ \nAM ELAA BA-E’EDIN FA-YATAJAHHAMONEE \nOr to a strange, and he will glower at me! \nاَمْ اِلَی الْمُسْتَضْعَفِیْنَ لِیْ \nAM ELAL MUSTAZA’FEENA LEE \nOr to those who deem me weak!\nوَ اَنْتَ رَبِّیْ وَ مَلِیْكُ اَمْرِیْ \nWA ANTA RABBEE WA MALEEKO AMREE \nWhile You are my Lord and the master of my affairs!\nاَشْكُوْ اِلَیْكَ غُرْبَتِیْ وَ بُعْدَ دَارِیْ \nASHKOO ELAYKA GURBATEE WA BO’DA DAAREE \nI complain to You about my alienation and my foreignness\nوَ هَوَانِیْ عَلٰی مَنْ مَلَّكْتَہٗ اَمْرِیْ \nWA HAWAANEE A’LAA MAN MALLAKTAHU AMREE \nand my ignominy in the eyes of him whom You have given domination over me.\nاِلٰهِیْ فَلَاْ تُحْلِلْ عَلَیَّ غَضَبَكَ \nELAAHEE FALAA TOHLIL A’LAYYA GHAZABAKA \nSo, O my God, do not make Your wrath come upon me.\nفَاِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ غَضِبْتَ عَلَیَّ فَلَاْ اُبَالِیْ \nFA-IN LAM TAKUN GHAZIBTA A’LAYYA FALAA OBAALEE \nIf You are not wrathful with me, then I care for nothing save You.\nسُبْحَانَكَ غَیْرَ اَنَّ عَافِیَتَكَ اَوْسَعُ لِیْ \nSUBHAANAKA GHAYRA ANNA A’AFEYATAKA AWSA-O’ LEE \nAll glory be to You; yet, Your granting me wellbeing is more favorable for me.\nفَاَسْئَلُكَ یَا رَبِّ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ \nFA-ASALOKA YAA RABBE BENOORE WAJHEKAL \nSo, I beseech You, O my Lord, in the name of the Light of Your Face\nالَّذِیْ اَشْرَقَتْ لَهُ الْاَرْضُ وَ السَّمٰوَاتُ \nLAZEE ASHRAQAT LAHUL ARZO WAS SAMAAWAATO \nto which the earth and the heavens have shone,\nوَ كُشِفَتْ بِهِ الظُّلُمَاتُ \nWA KOSHEFAT BEHIZ ZOLOMAATO \nby which all darkness has been uncovered,\nوَ صَلُحَ بِہٖ اَمْرُ الْاَوَّلِیْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِیْنَ \nWA SALOHA BEHI AMRUL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHEREENA \nand by which the affairs of the past and the coming generations are made right,\nاَنْ لَاْ تُمِیْتَنِیْ عَلٰی غَضَبِكَ \nAN LAA TOMEETANEE A’LAA GHAZABEKA \ndo not cause me to die while You are wrathful with me\nوَ لَاْ تُنْزِلَ بِیْ سَخَطَكَ \nWA LAA TUNZILA BEE SAKHATAKA \nand do not inflict on me Your rage.\nلَكَ الْعُتْبٰی لَكَ الْعُتْبٰی \nLAKAL U’TBAA LAKAL U’TBAA \nYou have the right to scold; You have the right to scold;\nحَتّٰی تَرْضٰیْ قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ لَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nHATTAA TARZAA QABLA ZAALEKA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA \nuntil You are pleased (with me) before that. There is no god save You;\nرَبَّ الْبَلَدِ الْحَرَامِ وَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ \nRABBAL BALADIL HARAAME WAL MASHA’RIL HARAAME \nLord of the Holy City, the Holy Monument,\nوَ الْبَیْتِ الْعَتِیْقِ الَّذِیْ اَحْلَلْتَهُ الْبَرَكَۃَ \nWAL BAYTIL A’TEEQIL LAZEE AHLALTAHUL BARAKATA \nand the Ancient House that You have encompassed with blessing\nوَ جَعَلْتَہٗ  لِلنَّاسِ اَمْنًا \nWA JA-A’LTAHU LINNAASE AMNAN \nand made security for people.\nیَا مَنْ عَفَا عَنْ عَظِیْمِ الذُّنُوْبِ بِحِلْمِہٖ \nYAA MAN A’FAA A’N A’ZEEMIZ ZONOOBE BEHILMEHI \nO He Who pardoned the grand sins by His forbearance!\nیَا مَنْ اَسْبَغَ النَّعْمَآءَ بِفَضْلِہٖ \nYAA MAN ASBAGHAN NA’MAAA-A BEFAZLEHI \nO He Who bestowed bounties by His favoring!\nیَا مَنْ اَعْطَی الْجَزِیْلَ بِكَرَمِہٖ \nYAA MAN A-A’TAL JAZEELA BEKARAMEHI \nO He Who gave in abundance by His generosity!\nیَا عُدَّتِیْ فِیْ شِدَّتِیْ وَ یَا صَاحِبِیْ فِیْ وَحْدَتِیْ \nYAA U’DDATEE FEE SHIDDATEE YAA SAAHEBEE FEE WAHDATEE \nO my means in my hardship! O my companion in my loneliness!\nیَا غِیَاثِیْ فِیْ كُرْبَتِیْ یَا وَلِیِّ فِیْ نِعْمَتِیْ \nYAA GHEYAASEE FEE KURBATEE YAA WALIYYEE FEE NEA’MATEE \nO my relief in my agony! O my Benefactor in my amenities!\nیَا اِلٰهِیْ وَ اِلٰهَ اٰبَآئِیْ \nYAA ELAAHEE WA ELAAHA AABAAA-EE \nO my God and the God of my forefathers:\nاِبْرَاهِیْمَ وَ اِسْمٰعِیْلَ وَ اِسْحٰقَ وَ یَعْقُوْبَ \nIBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA \nAbraham, Ishmael, Isaac, and Jacob;\nوَ رَبَّ جَبْرَئِیْلَ وَ مِیْكَائِیْلَ وَ اِسْرَافِیْلَ \nWA RABBA JABRA-EELA WA MEEKAA-EELA WA ISRAAFEELA \nthe Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Seraph;\nوَ رَبَّ مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِیِّیْنَ \nWA RABBA MOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA \nthe Lord of Muhammad, the Seal of Prophets,\nوَ اٰلِهِ الْمُنْتَجَبِیْنَ وَ مُنْزِلَ التَّوْرٰیۃِ وَ الْاِنْجِیْلِ \nWA AALEHIL MUNTAJABEENA WA MUNZELAT TAWRAATE WAL INJEELE \nand his elite Household; the Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel,\nوَ الزَّبُوْرِ وَ الْفُرْقَانِ \nWAZ ZABOORE WAL FURQAANE \nthe Psalms, and the Furqan;\nوَ مُنَزِّلَ کہٰٓیٰٓعٓصٓ و َطٰٓہٰ وَ یٰٓس \nWA MONAZZELA KAAAF-HAAA-YAAA-A’YN-SAAD WA TAAHAA WA YAAASIN \nthe Revealer of kaaf-haa-yaa-ayn-saad and Taa-haa, Yaa-seen,\nوَ الْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِیْمِ \nWAL QURNAAANIL HAKEEME \nand the Quran, full of wisdom.\nاَنْتَ كَهْفِيْ حِیْنَ تُعْیِیْنِيْ الْمَذَاهِبُ فِيْ سَعَتِهَا \nANTA KAHFEE HEENA TO’YEENIL MAZAAHEBO FEE SA-A’TEHAA \nYou are my haven when the wide courses fail to carry me\nوَ تَضِیْقُ بِیَ الْاَرْضُ بِرُحْبِهَا \nWA TAZEEQO BEYAL ARZO BEROHBEHAA \nand when the earth, despite its width, become too narrow to bear me.\nوَ لَوْلَاْ رَحْمَتُكَ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْهَالِكِیْنَ وَاَنْتَ مُقِیْلُ عَثْرَتِیْ \nWA LAWLAA RAHMATOKA LAKUNTO MENAL HAALEKEENA WA ANTA MOQEELO A’SRATEE \nWithout Your mercy, I would have been of those perishing. You overlook my slips;\nوَ لَوْلَاْ سَتْرُكَ اِیَّایَ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمَفْضُوْحِیْنَ \nWA LAWLAA SATROKA IYYAAYA LAKUNTO MENAL MAFZOOHEENA \nand without Your covering me, I would have been of those exposed.\nوَ اَنْتَ مُؤَیِّدِیْ بِالنَّصْرِ عَلٰی اَعْدَآئِیْ \nWA ANTA MOAYYEDEE BIN-NASRE A’LAA A-A’DAAA-EE \nYou aid me with Your support against my enemies;\nوَ لَوْلَاْ نَصْرُكَ اِیَّایَ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمَغْلُوْبِیْنَ \nWA LAWLAA NASROKA IYYAAYA LAKUNTO MENAL MAGHLOOBEENA \nand without Your support, I would have been of those overwhelmed.\nیَا مَنْ خَصَّ نَفْسَہٗ بِالسُّمُوِّ وَ الرِّفْعَۃِ \nYAA MAN KHASSA NAFSAHU BIS-SOMUWWE WAR RIF-A’TE \nO He Who gives Himself exclusively superiority and highness;\nفَاَوْلِیَآئُہٗ بِعِزِّہٖ یَعْتَزُّوْنَ \nFA-AWLEYAAA-OHU BE-I’ZZEHI YA’TAZZOONA \nso, His friends pride themselves on account of His pride.\nیَا مَنْ جَعَلَتْ لَهُ الْمُلُوْكُ نِیْرَ الْمَذَلَّۃِ عَلٰی اَعْنَاقِهِمْ \nYAA MAN JA-A’LAT LAHUL MOLOOKO NEERAL MAZALLATE A’LAA A-A’NAAQEHIM \nO He for Whom the kings put the yoke of humiliation on their necks;\nفَهُمْ مِنْ سَطَوَاتِہٖ خَآئِفُوْنَ \nFAHUM MIN SATAWAATEHI KHAA-EFOONA \nfor they are fearful of His authority.\nیَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَۃَ الْاَعْیُنِ وَ مَا تُخْفِیْ الصُّدُوْرُ \nYA’LAMO KHAA-ENATAL A-A’YONE WA MAA TUKHFIS SODOORO \nHe knows the stealthy looks of eyes and that which the breasts conceal\nوَ غَیْبَ مَا تَاْتِیْ بِهِ الْاَزْمِنَۃُ وَ الدُّهُوْرُ \nWA GHAYBA MAA TAATEE BEHIL AZMENATO WAD DOHOORO \nand the future of the times and ages.\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ یَعْلَمُ كَیْفَ هُوَ اِلَّا هُوَ \nYAA MAN LAA YA’LAMO KAYFA HOWA ILLAA HOWA \nO He save Whom none knows how He is!\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ یَعْلَمُ مَا هُوَ اِلَّا هُوَ \nYAA MAN LAA YA’LAMO MAA HOWA ILLAA HOWA \nO He save Whom none knows what He is!\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ يعَلْمُ مَا یَعْلَمُہٗ اِلَّا هُوَ \nYAA MAN LAA YA’LAMO MAA YA’LAMOHU ILLAA HOWA \nO He save Whom none knows what He knows!\nیَا مَنْ كَبَسَ الْاَرْضَ عَلَی الْمَآءِ \nYAA MAN KABASAL ARZA A’LAL MAAA-E \nO He Who surfaced the earth over the water\nوَ سَدَّ الْهَوَآءَ بِالسَّمَآءِ یَا مَنْ لَہٗ اَكْرَمُ الْاَسْمَآءِ \nWA SADDAL HAWAAA-A BIS-SAMAAA-E YAA MAN LAHU AKRAMUL ASMAAA-E \nand blocked the air with the heavens! O He Who has the noblest of names!\nیَا ذَالْمَعْرُوْفِ الَّذِیْ لَاْ یَنْقَطِعُ اَبَدًا \nYAA ZAL MA’ROOFIL LAZEE LAA YANQATE-O’ ABADAN \nO Owner of favor that is never interrupted!\nیَا مُقَیِّضَ الرَّكْبِ لِیُوْسُفَ فِی الْبَلَدِ الْقَفْرِ \nYAA MOQAYYEZAR RAKBE LE-YOOSOFA FIL BALADIL QAFRE \nO He Who directed the caravan towards Joseph in the wasteland,\nوَ مُخْرِجَہٗ مِنَ الْجُبِّ وَ جَاعِلَہٗ بَعْدَ الْعُبُوْدِیَّۃِ مَلِکًا \nWA MUKHREJAHU MENAL JUBBE WA JAA-E’LAHU BA’DAL O’BOODIYYATE MALEKAN \ntook him out of the pit, and made him king after enslavement!\nیَارَآدَّہٗ عَلٰی یَعْقُوْبَ \nYAA RAAAD-DAHU A’LAA YA’QOOBA \nO He Who had returned him to Jacob\nبَعْدَ اَنِ ابْیَضَّتْ عَیْنَاهُ مِنَ الْحُزْنِ فَهُوَ كَظِیْمٌ \nBA’DA ANIB YAZZAT A’YNAAHO MENAL HUZNE FAHOWA KAZEEMUN \nafter his eyes became white on account of the grief, and he was a repressor of grief!\nیَا كَاشِفَ الضُّرِّ وَالْبَلْوٰی عَنْ اَیُّوْبَ \nYAA KAASHEFAZ ZURRE WAL BALWAA A’N AYYOOBA \nO He Who removed the distress and misfortune from Job\nوَ مُمْسِكَ یَدَیْ اِبْرَاهِیْمَ عَنْ ذَبْحِ ابْنِہٖ \nWA MUMSEKA YADAY IBRAAHEEMA A’N ZABHIB NEHI \nand withheld the hands of Abraham from slaying his son\nبَعْدَ كِبَرِ سِنِّہٖ وَ فَنَآءِ عُمُرِہٖ \nBA’DA KEBARE SINNEHI WA FANAAA-E O’MOREHI \nafter his old age and termination of his lifetime!\nیَا مَنِ اسْتَجَابَ لِزَكَرِیَّا فَوَهَبَ لَہٗ یَحْیٰی \nYAA MANIS TAJAABA LEZAKARIYYAA FAWAHABA LAHU YAHYAA \nO He Who responded to Zachariah and granted him John\nوَ لَمْ یَدَعْهُ فَرْدًا وَحِیْدًا \nWA LAM YADA’HO FARDAN WAHEEDAN \nwithout leaving him alone and lonely!\nیَا مَنْ اَخْرَجَ یُوْنُسَ مِنْ بَطْنِ الْحُوْتِ \nYAA MAN AKHRAJA YOONOSA MIN BATNIL HOOTE \nO He Who took Jonah out of the belly of the big fish!\nیَا مَنْ فَلَقَ الْبَحْرَ لِبَنِیْ اِسْرَآئِیْلَ \nYAA MAN FALAQAL BAHRA LEBANEE ISRAAA-EELA \nO He Who cleft the sea to the children of Israel;\nفَاَنْجَاهُمْ وَ جَعَلَ فِرْعُوْنَ وَ جُنُوْدَہٗ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِیْنَ \nFA-ANJAAHUM WA JA-A’LA FIR-A’WNA WA JONOODAHU MENAL MUGHRAQEENA \nso, He saved them and made Pharaoh and his army of the drowned!\nیَا مَنْ اَرْسَلَ الرِّیَاحَ مُبَشِّرَاتٍۢ بَیْنَ یَدَیْ رَحْمَتِہٖ \nYAA MAN ARSALAR REYAAHA MOBASH-SHERAATIM BAYNA YADAY RAHMATEHI \nO He Who sent the winds, bearing good news, before His mercy!\nیَا مَنْ لَمْ یَعْجَلْ عَلٰی مَنْ عَصَاهُ مِنْ خَلْقِہٖ \nYAA MAN LAM YA’JAL A’LAA MAN A’SAAHO MIN KHALQEHI \nO He Who has no hastiness on His creatures who disobey Him!\nیَا مَنِ سْتَنْقَذَ السَّحَرَۃَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ طُوْلِ الْجُحُوْدِ \nYAA MANIS TANQAZAS SAHARATA MIM BA’DE TOOLIL JOHOODE \nO He Who saved the sorcerers after their long denial!\nوَ قَدْ غَدَوْ فِیْ نِعْمَتِہٖ \nWA QAD GHADAW FEE NE’MATEHI \nand after they had lived in His bounty,\nیَاْكُلُوْنَ رِزْقَہٗ وَ یَعْبُدُوْنَ غَیْرَہٗ \nYAAKOLOONA RIZQAHU WA YA’BODOONA GHAYRAHU \neating from His sustenance, but serving someone else other than Him,\nوَ قَدْ حَآدُّوْهُ وَ نَآدُّوْهُ \nWA QAD HAADDOOHO WA NAADDOOHO \nacting in opposition to Him, antagonizing Him,\nوَ كَذَّبُوْا رُسُلَہٗ یَا اَﷲُ یَا اَﷲُ یَا بَدِیْءُ \nWA KAZZABOO ROSOLAHU YAA ALLAAHO YAA ALLAAHO YAA BADEE-O \nand denying His messengers. O Allah! O Allah! O Originator!\nیَا بَدِیْعُ لَاْ نِدَّ لَكَ یَا دَآئِمًا لَاْ نَفَادَ لَكَ \nYAA BADEE-O’ LAA NIDDA LAKA YAA DAAA-EMAN LAA NAFAADA LAKA \nO Fashioner! There is no equal to You. O Everlasting! There is no end to You.\nیَا حَیًّا حِیْنَ لَاْ حَیَّ یَا مُحْیِی الْمَوْتٰی \nYAA HAYYAN HEENA LAA HAYYA YAA MOHAYEYAL MAWTAA \nO Ever-living when there was no living thing! O Raiser from the dead!\nیَا مَنْ هُوَ قَآئِمٌ عَلٰی كُلِّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ \nYAA MAN HOWA QAAA-EMUN A’LAA KULLE NAFSIN BEMAA KASABAT \nO He Who watches every soul as to what it earns!\nیَا مَنْ قَلَّ لَہٗ شُكْرِیْ فَلَمْ  یَحْرِمْنِیْ \nYAA MAN QALLA LAHU SHUKRE FALAM YAHRIMNEE \nO He to Whom I rarely turned thankful; yet, He did not deprive me,\nوَ عَظُمَتْ خَطِیْئَتِیْ فَلَمْ یَفْضَحْنِیْ \nWA A’ZOMAT KHATEE-ATEE FALAM YAFZAHNEE \nagainst Whom I committed grand sins; yet, He did not disclose me,\nوَ رَاٰنِیْ عَلَی الْمَعَاصِیْ فَلَمْ یَشْهَرْنِیْ \nWA RA-AANEE A’LAL MA-A’ASEE FALAM YASH-HARNEE \nand Who saw me insisting on disobeying Him; yet, He did not divulge me.\nیَا مَنْ حَفِظَنِیْ فِیْ صِغَرِیْ \nYAA MAN HAFEZANEE FEE SEGHAREE \nO He Who safeguarded me in my early life!\nیَا مِنْ رَزَقَنِیْ فِیْ كِبَرِیْ \nYAA MAN RAZAQANEE FEE KEBAREE \nO He Who provided me with sustenance in my old age!\nیَا مَنْ اَیَادِیْهِ عِنْدِیْ لَاْ تُحْصٰی وَ نِعَمُہٗ لَاْ تُجَازٰی \nYAA MAN AYAADEEHE I’NDEE LAA TOHSAA WA NE-A’MOHU LAA TOJAAZAA \nO He Whose favors to me are innumerable and Whose bounties cannot be compensated!\nیَا مَنْ عَارَضَنِیْ بِالْخَیْرِ وَ الْاِحْسَانِ \nYAA MAN A’ARAZANEE BIL-KHAYRE WAL EHSANE \nO He Who receives me with good turn and kindness\nوَ عَارَضْتُہٗ بِالْاِسَآئَۃِ وَ الْعِصْیَانِ \nWA A’ARAZTOHU BIL-ESAA-ATE WAL I’SYAANE \nbut I meet Him with offense and disobedience!\nیَا مَنْ هَدَانِیْ لِلْاِیْمَانِ \nYAA MAN HADAANEE LIL-EEMAANE \nO He Who had guided me to faith\nمِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ اَعْرِفَ شُكْرَ الْاِمْتِنَانِ \nMIN QABLE AN A-A’REFA SHUKRAL IMTENAANE \nbefore I learnt showing gratitude!\nیَا مَنْ دَعَوْتُہٗ مَرِیْضًا فَشَفَانِیْ \nYAA MAN DA-A’WTOHU MAREEZAN FASHAFAANEE \nO He Whom I besought in sickness; so, He restored me to health,\nوَ عُرْیَانًا فَكَسَانِیْ وَ جَآئِعًا فَاَشْبَعَنِیْ \nWA U’RYAANAN FAKASAANEE WA JAAA-E-A’N FA-ASHBA-A’NEE \nin bareness; so, He covered me, in hunger; so, He satiated me,\nوَ عَطْشَانَ فَاَرْوَانِیْ وَ ذَلِیْلًا فَاَعَزَّنِیْ \nWA A’TSHAANAN FA-ARWAANEE WA ZALEELAN FA-A-A’ZZANEE \nin thirst; so, He quenched my thirst, in humility; so, He granted me dignity,\nوَ جَاهِلًا فَعَرَّفَنِیْ وَ وَحِیْدًا فَكَثَّرَنِیْ \nWA JAAHELAN FA-A’RRAFANEE WA WAHEEDAN FAKASSARANEE \nin ignorance; so, He taught me, in loneliness; so, He increased my number,\nوَ غَائِبًا فَرَدَّنِیْ \nWA GHAAEBAN FARADDANEE \nin foreignness absence; so, He returned me home,\nوَ مُقِلًّا فَاَغْنَانِیْ وَ مُنْتَصِرًا فَنَصَرَنِیْ \nWA MOQILLAN FA-AGHNAANEE WA MUNTASERAN FA-NASARANEE \nin poverty; so, He enriched me, in victory-seeking; so, He supported me,\nوَ غَنِیًّا فَلَمْ یَسْلُبْنِیْ \nWA GHANIYYAN FALAM YASLUBNEE \nand in richness; so, He did not deprive me.\nوَ اَمْسَكْتُ عَنْ جَمِیْعِ ذٰلِكَ فَابْتَدَاَنِیْ \nWA AMSAKTO A’N JAMEE-E’ ZAALEKA FABTADA-ANEE \nWhen I withheld praying Him in all these situation, He took the initiative.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَ الشُّكْرُ یَا مَنْ اَقَالَ عَثْرَتِیْ \nFALAKAL HAMDO WASH-SHUKRO YAA MAN AQAALA A’SRATEE \nSo, all praise and thanks be to You; O He Who overlooked my slips,\nوَ نَفَّسَ كُرْبَتِیْ وَ اَجَابَ دَعْوَتِیْ \nWA NAFFASA KURBATEE WA AJAABA DA’WATEE \nrelieved my agonies, responded to my prayer,\nوَ سَتَرَ عَوْرَتِیْ وَ غَفَرَ ذُنُوْبِیْ \nWA SATARA A’WRATEE WA GHAFARA ZONOOBEE \ncovered my flaws, forgave my sins,\nوَ بَلَّغَنِیْ طَلِبَتِیْ وَ نَصَرَنِیْ عَلٰی عَدُوِّیْ \nWA BALLAGHANEE TALEBATEE WA NASARANEE A’LAA A’DUWWEE\nsettled my need, and supported me against my enemy.\nوَ اِنْ اَعُدَّ نِعَمَكَ وَ مِنَنَكَ وَ كَرَائِمَ مِنَحِكَ لَاْ اُحْصِیْهَا \nWA IN A-U’DDO NE-A’MAKA WA MENANAKA WA KARAA-EMA MENAHEKA LAA OHSEEHAA \nIf I count Your bounties, favors, and liberal gifts, I will never number them.\nیَا مَوْلَایَ اَنْتَ الَّذِیْ مَنَنْتَ \nYAA MAWLAAYA ANTAL LAZEE MANANTA \nO my Master! It is You Who bestowed (upon me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَنْعَمْتَ اَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَحْسَنْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AN-A’MTA ANTAL LAZEE AHSANTA \nIt is You Who conferred favors (upon me). It is You Who did good (to me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَجْمَلْتَ اَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَفْضَلْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AJMALTA ANTAL LAZEE AFZALTA \nIt is You Who treated (me) excellently. It is You Who favored (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَكْمَلْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AKMALTA \nIt is You Who perfected (Your blessings upon me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ رَزَقْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE RAZAQTA \nIt is You Who provided (me) with sustenance.\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ وَفَّقْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE WAFFAQTA \nIt is You Who led (me) to success. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَعْطَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A-A’TAYTA \nIt is You Who gave (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَغْنَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AGHNAYTA \nIt is You Who enriched (me). \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَقْنَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AQNAYTA \nIt is You Who gave (me) to hold.\nاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اٰوَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AAWAYTA \nIt is You Who gave (me) shelter. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ كَفَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE KAFAYTA \nIt is You Who saved (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ هَدَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE HADAYTA \nIt is You Who guided (me). \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ عَصَمْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A’SAMTA \nIt is You Who protected (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ سَتَرْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE SATARTA \nIt is You Who covered my faults. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ غَفَرْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE GHAFARTA \nIt is You Who forgave (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَقَلْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AQALTA \nIt is You Who overlooked my sins. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ مَكَنْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE MAKKANTA \nIt is You Who established (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَعْزَزْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A-A’ZAZTA \nIt is You Who consolidated (me). \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَعَنْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A-A’NTA \nIt is You Who helped (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ عَضَدْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A’ZADTA \nIt is You Who backed (me) up. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَیَّدْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AYYADTA \nIt is You Who aided (me).\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ نَصَرْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE NASARTA \nIt is You Who supported (me). \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ شَفَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE SHAFAYTA \nIt is You Who restored (me) to health.\nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ عَافَیْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE A’AFAYTA \nIt is You Who granted (me) wellbeing. \nاَنْتَ الَّذِیْ اَكْرَمْتَ \nANTAL LAZEE AKRAMTA \nIt is You Who honored (me).\nتَبَارَكْتَ وَ تَعَالَیْتَ \nTABAARAKTA WA TA-A’ALAYTA \nBlessed be You and Exalted be You. \nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ دَآئِمًا \nFALAKAL HAMDO DAAA-EMAN \nSo, all praise be to You permanently,\nوَ لَكَ الشُّكْرُ وَاصِبًا اَبَدًا \nWA LAKASH SHUKRO WAASEBAN ABADAN \nand all thanks be to You enduringly and eternally.\nثُمَّ اَنَا یَا اِلٰهِیْ الْمُعْتَرِفُ بِذُنُوْبِیْ \nSUMMA ANAA YAA ELAAHIL MO’TAREFO BEZONOOBEE \nHowever, it is I, O my God, who confess of my sins;\nفَاغْفِرْ هَالِیْ \nFAGHFIR HAALEE \nso, forgive them to me. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ اَسَاْتُ \nANAL LAZEE ASAATO \nIt is I who did badly.\nاَنَا الَّذِیْ اَخْطَاْتُ \nANAL LAZEE AKH-TAATO \nIt is I who did wrong. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ هَمَمْتُ \nANAL LAZEE HAMAMTO \nIt is I who had evil intention.\nاَنَا الَّذِیْ جَهِلْتُ \nANAL LAZEE JAHILTO \nIt is I who acted impolitely. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ غَفَلْتُ \nANAL LAZEE GHAFALTO \nIt is I who was inadvertent.\nاَنَا الَّذِیْ سَهَوْتُ \nANAL LAZEE SAHAWTO \nIt is I who was inattentive. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ اعْتَمَدْتُ \nANAL LAZEE’ TAMADTO \nIt is I who leaned (on something other than You).\nاَنَا الَّذِیْ تَعَمَّدْتُ \nANAL LAZEE TA-A’MMADTO \nIt is I who did wrong deliberately. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ وَعَدْتُ \nANAL LAZEE WA-A’DTO \nIt is I who promised.\nوَ اَنَا الَّذِیْ اَخْلَفْتُ \nANAL LAZEE AKHLAFTO \nIt is I who failed to fulfill it. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ نَكَثْتُ \nANAL LAZEE NAKASTO \nIt is I who breached. \nاَنَا الَّذِیْ اَقْرَرْتُ \nANAL LAZEE AQRARTO \nIt is I who confessed.\nاَنَا الَّذِیْ اعْتَرَفْتُ بِنِعْمَتِكَ عَلَیَّ وَ عِنْدِیْ \nANAL LAZEE’ TARAFTO BE-NE’MATEKA A’LAYYA WA I’NDEE \nIt is I who testified to Your favors upon and with me,\nوَ اَبُوْءُ بِذُنُوْبِیْ فَاغْفِرْهَا لِیْ \nWA ABOO-O BEZONOOBEE FAGHFIRHAA LEE \nand I now acknowledge of my sins; so, forgive them to me.\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ تَضُرُّہٗ ذُنُوْبُ عِبَادِہٖ \nYAA MAN LAA TAZURROHU ZONOOBO E’BAADEHI \nO He Who is not injured by the sins of His servants,\nوَ هُوَ الْغَنِیُّ عَنْ طَاعَتِهِمْ \nWA HOWAL GHANIYYO A’N TAA-A’TEHIM \nand Who can surely do without their obedience,\nوَ الْمُوَفِّقُ مَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْهُمْ \nWAL MOWAFFEQO MAN A’MELA SAALEHAM MINHUM \nand Who inspires those of them to do good,\nبِمَعُوْنَتِہٖ وَ رَحْمَتِہٖ \nBEMA-O’ONATEHI WA RAHMATEHI \nout of His aid and mercy. \nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ اِلٰهِیْ وَ سَیِّدِیْ \nFALAKAL HAMDO ELAAHEE WA SAYYEDEE \nSo, all praise be to You, O my God and my Master.\nاِلٰهِیْ اَمَرْتَنِیْ فَعَصَیْتُكَ \nELAAHEE AMARTANEE FA-A’SAYTOKA \nO my God: You ordered me, but I disobeyed You. \nوَ نَهَیْتَنِیْ فَارْتَكَبْتُ نَهْیَكَ \nWA NAHAYTANEE FARTAKABTO NAHYAKA \nYou warned me, but I violated Your warning\nفَاَصْبَحْتُ لَاْ ذَا بَرَآئَۃٍ لِّیْ فَاَعْتَذِرُ \nFA-ASBAHTO LAA ZAA BARAAA-ATIL LEE FA-A-A’TAZERO \nSo, I am now lacking neither justification to apologize\nوَ لَاْ ذَا قُوَّۃٍ فَاَنْتَصِرُ \nWA LAA ZAA QUWWATIN FA-ANTASERO\nnor power to support myself. \nفَبِاَیِّ شَیْءٍ اَسْتَقْبِلُكَ یَا مَوْلَایَ \nFABEAYYE SHAY-IN ASTAQBELOKA YAA MAWLAAYA \nBy which thing can I now meet You, O my Master?\nاَبِسَمْعِیْ اَمْ بِبَصَرِیْ اَمْ بِلِسَانِیْ اَمْ بِیَدِیْ اَمْ بِرِجْلِیْ \nA BESAM-E’E AM BE-BASAREE AM BELESAANEE AM BEYADEE AM BERIJLEE \nIs it by my hearing, my sight, my tongue, my hand, or my foot?\nاَلَیْسَ كُلُّهَا نِعَمَكَ عِنْدِیْ \nA LAYSA KULLOHAA NE-A’MAKA I’NDEE \nAre all these not Your bounties on me\nوَ بِكُلِّهَا عَصَیْتُكَ یَا مَوْلَایَ \nWA BEKULLEHAA A’SAYTOKA YAA MAWLAAYA \nand with all of them I have disobeyed You, O my Master?\nفَلَكَ الْحُجَّۃُ وَ السَّبِیْلُ عَلَیَّ \nFALAKAL HUJJATO WAS SABEELO A’LAYYA \nYou have absolute argument and claim against me.\nیَا مَنْ سَتَرَنِیْ مِنَ الْاٰبَآءِ وَ الْاُمَّهَاتِ اَنْ یَزْجُرُوْنِیْ \nYAA MAN SATARANEE MENAL AAABAAA-E WAL UMMAHAATE AN YAZJOROONEE \nO He Who covered me from fathers and mothers lest they might have driven me away,\nوَ مِنَ الْعَشَائِرِ وَ الْاِخْوَانِ اَنْ یُعَیِّرُوْنِیْ \nWA MENAL A’SHAA-ERE WAL IKHWAANE AN YO-A’YYEROONEE \nfrom relatives and friends lest they might have gibed me,\nوَ مِنَ السَّلَاطِیْنِ اَنْ یُعَاقِبُوْنِیْ وَ لَوِاطَّلَعُوْا یَا مَوْلَایَ \nWA MENAS SALAATEENE AN YO-A’AQEBOONEE WA LAWIT TALAO’O YAA MAWLAAYA \nand from rulers lest they might have punished me.  Had they, O my Master, seen\nعَلٰی مَا اطَّلَعْتَ عَلَیْهِ مِنِّیْ اِذًا مَّا اَنْظَرُوْنِیْ \nA’LAA MAT TALA’TA A’LAYHE MINNEE EZAM MAA ANZAROONEE \nthat which You knew about me, they would certainly have granted me no respite\nوَ لَرَفَضُوْنِیْ وَ قَطَعُوْنِیْ \nWA LARAFAZOONEE WA QATAO’ONEE \nand they would have rejected and parted company with me.\nفَهَا اَنَا ذَا یَا اِلٰهِیْ بَیْنَ یَدَیْكَ یَا سَیِّدِیْ \nFAHAA ANAA ZAA YAA ELAAHEE BAYNA YADAYKA YAA SAYYEDEE \nHere I am now, O my God, between Your hands, O my Master,\nخَاضِعٌ ذَلِیْلٌ حَصِیْرٌ حَقِیْرٌ \nKHAAZE-U’N ZALEELUN HASEERUN HAQEERUN \nsubmissive, humble, helpless, and worthless.\nلَاْ ذُوْ بَرَآئَۃٍ فَاعْتَذِرُ \nLAA ZOO BARAAA-ATIN FA’TAZERO \nI am now lacking neither justification to apologize\nوَ لَاْ ذُوْقُوَّۃٍ فَاَنْتَصِرَ \nWA LAA ZOO QUWWATIN FAN-TASERA \nnor power to support myself, \nوَ لَاْ حُجَّۃٍ فَاَحْتَجُّ بِهَا \nWA LAA HUJJATIN FA-AHTAJJO BEHAA \nnor excuse to advance as a plea,\nوَ لَاْ قَآئِلٌ لَمْ اَجْتَرِحْ وَ لَمْ اَعْمَلْ سُوْٓ ءً \nWA LAA QAAA-ELUN LAM AJTAREH WA LAM A-A’MAL SOOO-AN \nnor can I claim not committing and not acting badly.\nوَ مَا عَسَی الْجُحُوْدُ وَ لَوْ جَحَدْتُ یَا مَوْلَایَ یَنْفَعُنِیْ \nWA MAA A’SAL JOHOODO WA LAW JAHADTO YAA MAWLAAYA YANFA-O’NEE \nHow can denial, if I deny, O my Master, serve me?\nكَیْفَ وَ اَنّٰی ذٰلِكَ \nKAYFA WA ANNAA ZAALEKA \nHow and in what manner can I do so,\nوَ جَوَارِحِیْ كُلُّهَا شَاهِدَۃٌ عَلَیَّ بِمَا قَدْ عَمِلْتُ \nWA JAWAAREHEE KULLAHAA SHAHEDATUN A’LAYYA BEMAA QAD A’MILTO \nwhile all my organs are witnesses for what I did?\nوَ عَلِمْتُ یَقِیْنًا غَیْرَ ذِیْ شَكٍّ \nWA A’LIMTO YAQEENAN GHAYRA ZEE SHAKKIN \nI know for sure and without doubt\nاَنَّكَ سَآئِلِیْ مِنْ عَظَائِمِ الْاُمُوْرِ \nANNAKA SAAA-ELEE MIN A’ZAAEMIL OMOORE \nthat You will interrogate me about these grand matter,\nوَ اَنَّكَ الْحَكَمُ الْعَدْلُ الَّذِیْ لَاْ تَجُوْرُ \nWA ANNAKAL HAKAMUL A’DLUL LAZEE LAA TAJOORO \nYou are the Just Judge Who never wrongs,\nوَ عَدْلُكَ مُهْلِكِیْ وَ مِنْ كُلِّ عَدْلِكَ مَهْرَبِیْ \nWA A’DLOKA MOHLEKEE WA MIN KULLE A’DLEKA MAHRABEE \nYour justice will ruin me, and from Your all justice I flee.\nفَاِنْ تُعَذِّبْنِیْ یَا اِلٰهِیْ \nFA-IN TO-A’ZZIBNEE YAA ELAAHEE \nIf You, O my God, chastise me,\nفَبِذُنُوْبِیْ بَعْدَ حُجَّتِكَ عَلَیَّ \nFABEZONOOBEE BA’DA HUJJATEKA A’LAYYA \nthen it is because of my sins after Your claim against me;\nوَ اِنْ تَعْفُ عَنِّیْ \nWA IN TA’FO A’NNEE \nand if You pardon me,\nفَبِحِلْمِكَ وُ جُوْدِكَ وَ كَرَمِكَ \nFABEHILMEKA WA JOODEKA WA KARAMEKA \nthen it is on account of Your forbearance, magnanimity, and generosity.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAZ ZAALEMEENA \nI have been of the wrongdoers. \nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُسْتَغْفِرِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL MUSTAGHFEREENA \nI have been of those seeking forgiveness.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُوَحِّدِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL MOWAHHEDEENA \nI have been of those professing Your Oneness.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْخَآئِفِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL KHAAA-EFEENA \nI have been of the fearful.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْوَجِلِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL WAJELEENA \nI have been of the apprehensive.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الرَّاجِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAR RAAJEENA \nI have been of those hoping (for You).\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الرَّاغِبِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAR RAAGHEBEENA \nI have been of those desiring (for You).\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُهَلِّلِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL MOHALLELEENA \nI have been of those professing that there is no god save You.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ السَّآئِلِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAS SAAA-ELEENA \nI have been of those beseeching (You).\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL MOSABBEHEENA \nI have been of those glorifying (You).\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You. \nاِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُكَبِّرِیْنَ \nINNEE KUNTO MENAL MOKABBEREENA \nI have been of those professing that You are the Greatest.\nلَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA \nThere is no god save You. All glory be to You.\nرَبِّی وَ رَبُّ اٰبَآئِیَ الْاَوَّلِیْنَ \nRABBEE WA RABBO AABAAA-EYAL AWWALEENA \nYou are my Lord and the Lord of my bygone fathers.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ہٰذَا ثَنَآئِیْ عَلَیْكَ مُمَجِّدًا \nALLAAHUMMA HAAZAA SANAAA-EE A’LAYKA MOMAJJEDAN \nO Allah, this is my praise for You, celebrating Your glory,\nوَ اِخْلَاصِیْ لِذِكْرِكَ مُوَحِّدًا \nWA IKHLAASEE LEZIKREKA MOWAHHEDAN \nmy sincerity to mention You and profess Your Oneness,\nوَ اِقْرَارِیْ بِاٰلَآئِكَ مُعَدِّدًا \nWA IQRAAREE BE-AA-LAAA-EKA MO-A’DDEDAN \nand my acknowledgment of Your bounties, counting them,\nوَ اِنْ كُنْتُ مُقِرًّا اَنِّیْ لَمْ اُحْصِهَا \nWA IN KUNTO MOQIRRAN ANNEE LAM OH-SEHAA \nalthough I confess that I could never count them\nلِكَثْرَتِهَا وَ سُبُوْعِهَا وَ تَظَاهُرِهَا وَ تَقَادُمِهَا اِلٰی حَادِثٍ \nLEKASRATEHAA WA SOBOO-E’HAA WA TAZAAHOREHAA WA TAQAADOMEHAA ELAA HAADESIN \nfor they are innumerable, abundant, continuous, and prior to a certain event.\nمَا لَمْ تَزَلْ تَتَعَهَدُنِیْ بِہٖ مَعَهَا \nMAA LAM TAZAL TATA-A’H-HADONEE BEHI MA-A’HAA \nYou have been conferring upon me with these bounties\nمُنْذُ خَلَقْتَنِیْ وَ بَرَاتَنِیْ مِنْ اَوَّلِ الْعُمْرِ \nMUNZO KHALAQTANEE WA BARAATANEE MIN AWWALIL U’MRE \nsince You created and originated me from the beginning of my age\nمِنَ الْاَغْنَاءِ مِنَ الْفَقْرِ وَ كَشْفِ الضُّرِّ \nMENAL AGHNAAA-E MENAL FAQRE WA KASHFIZ ZURRE \nthrough meeting my poverty relieving me from harm,\nوَ تَسْبِیْبِ الْیُسْرِ وَ دَفْعِ الْعُسْرِ \nWA TASBEEBIL YUSRE WA DAF-I’L U’SRE \ngiving me means of easiness, repelling misery from me,\nوَ تَفْرِیْجِ الْكَرْبِ وَ الْعَافِیَۃِ فِیْ الْبَدَنِ \nWA TAFREEJIL KARBE WAL A’AFEYATE FIL BADANE \nalleviating my agonies, granting me wellbeing in my body,\nوَ السَّلَامَۃِ فِیْ الدِّیْنِ \nWAS SALAAMATE FID DEENE \nand furnishing me with sound faith.\nوَ لَوْرَفَدَنِیْ عَلٰی قَدْرِ ذِكْرِ نِعْمَتِكَ جَمِیْعُ الْعَالَمِیْنَ \nWA LAW RAFADANEE A’LAA QADRE ZIKRE NE’MATEKA JAMEE-U’L A’ALAMEENA \nIf all creatures assist me to be able to mention Your bounties,\nمِنَ الْاَوَّلِیْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِیْنَ \nMENAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHEREENA \nincluding the past and the coming generations,\nمَا قَدَرْتُ وَ لَاْ هُمْ عَلٰی ذٰلِكَ تَقَدَّسْتَ وَ تَعَالَیْتَ \nMAA QADARTO WA LAA HUM A’LAA ZAALEKA TAQADDASTA WA TA-A’ALAYTA \nneither I nor will they be able to do that. Holy be You and Exalted be You;\nمِنْ رَّبِّ كَرِیْمٍ عَظِیْمٍ رَّحِیْمٍ \nMIR RABBE KAREEMIN A’ZEEMIR RAHEEMIN \nYou are All-generous, All-great, and All-merciful Sustainer.\nلَاْ تُحْصٰی اٰلَآؤُكَ وَ لَاْ یَبْلُغُ ثَنَآؤُكَ \nLAA TOHSAA AA-LAAA-OKA WA LAA YUBLAGHO SANAAA-OKA \nYour bounties are innumerable, (proper) praise of You is unreachable,\nوَ لَاْ تُكَافٰی نَعْمَآؤُكَ \nWA LAA TOKAAFAA NA’MAAA-OKA \nand Your graces cannot be rewarded.\nصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nsend blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَ اَتْمِمْ عَلَیْنَا نِعَمَكَ وَ اَسْعِدْنَا بِطَاعَتِكَ \nWA ATMIM A’LAYNAA NE-A’MAKA WA AS-I’DNAA BE-TAA-A’TEKA \nperfect Your bounties for us, and make us happy by obeying You.\nسُبْحَانَكَ لَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nSUBHAANAKA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA \nAll glory be to You. There is no god save You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ تُجِیْبُ الْمُضْطَرَّ \nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA TOJEEBUL MUZTARRA \nO Allah, verily, You answer the distressed,\nوَ تَكْشِفُ السُّوْٓ ءَ وَ تُغِیْثُ الْمَكْرُوْبَ \nWA TAKSHEFUS SOOO-A WA TOGHEESUL MAKROOBA \nremove the evil, aid the anguished,\nوَ تَشْفِیْ السَّقِیْمَ وَ تُغْنِيْ الْفَقِیْرَ \nWA TASHFIS SAQEEMA WA TUGHNIL FAQEERA \ncure the ailed, enrich the poor,\nوَ تَجْبُرُ الْكَسِیْرَ وَ تَرْحَمُ الصَّغِیْرَ \nWA TAJBORUL KASEERA WA TARHAMUS SAGHEERA \nset the broken, have mercy on the young,\nوَ تُعِیْنُ الْكَبِیْرَ وَ لَیْسَ دُوْنَكَ ظَهِیْرٌ \nWA TO-E’ENUL KABEERA WA LAYSA DOONAKA ZAHEERUN \nhelp the old, none can help against You,\nوَ لَاْ فَوْقَكَ قَدِیْرٌ وَ اَنْتَ الْعَلِیُّ الْكَبِیْرُ \nWA LAA FAWQAKA QADEERUN WA ANTAL A’LIYYUL KABEERO \nnone is more powerful than You, and You are the Most High, the All-great.\nیَا مُطْلِقَ الْمُكَبَّلِ الْاَسِیْرِ یَا رَازِقَ الطِّفْلِ الصَّغِیْرِ \nYAA MUTLEQAL MOKABBALIL ASEERE YAA RAAZEQAT TIFLIS SAGHEERE \nO He Who release the shackled captive! O He Who provides sustenance to the young child!\nیَا عِصْمَۃَ الْخَآئِفِ الْمُسْتَجِیْرِ \nYAA I’SMATAL KHAAA-EFIL MUSTAJEERE \nO He Who is the Preserver of the afraid seeker of refuge!\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ شَرِیْكَ لَہٗ وَ لَاْ وَزِیْرَ \nYAA MAN LAA SHAREEKA LAHU WA LAA WAZEERA \nO He Who has neither partner nor assistant,\nصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nsend blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَ اَعْطِنِیْ فِیْ ہٰذِهِ الْعَشِیَّۃِ اَفْضَلَ مَا اَعْطَیْتَ وَ اَنَلْتَ \nWA A-A’TENEE FEE HAAZEHIL A’SHIYYATE AFZALA MAA A-A’TAYTA WA ANALTA \nand grant me, in this evening, the best of what You have granted and awarded\nاَحَدًا مِّنْ عِبَادِكَ مِنْ نِعْمَۃٍ تُوْلِیْهَا \nAHADAM MIN E’BAADEKA MIN NE’MATIN TOOLEEHAA \nto any of Your servants, including a grace that You donate,\nوَ اٰلَآءٍ تُجَدِّدُهَا وَ بَلِیَّۃٍ تَصْرِفُهَا \nWA AA-LAAA-IN TOJADDEDOHAA WA BALIYYATIN TASREFOHAA \nbounties that You re-offer, a tribulation that You deter,\nوَ كُرْبَۃٍ تَكْشِفُهَا وَ دَعْوَۃٍ تَسْمَعُهَا \nWA KURBATIN TAKSHEFOHAA WA DA’WATIN TASMA-O’HAA \nan anguish that You remove, a prayer that You answer,\nوَ حَسَنَۃٍ تَتَقَبَّلُهَا وَ سَیِّئَۃٍ تَتَغَمَّدُهَا \nWA HASANATIN TATAQABBALOHAA WA SAYYE-ATIN TATAGHAMMADOHAA \na good deed that You admit, and an evildoing that You screen.\nاِنَّكَ لَطِیْفٌ بِمَا تَشَآءُ خَبِیْرٌ \nINNAKA LATEEFUN BEMAA TASHAAA-O KHABEERUN \nVerily, You are All-tender to him You will, and All-aware,\nوَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nand You have power over all things.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ اَقْرَبُ مَنْ دُعِیَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA AQRABO MIN DO-E’YA \nO Allah, Verily, You are the nearest of those whom are prayed,\nوَ اَسْرَعُ مَنْ اَجَابَ \nWA ASRA-O’ MAN AJAABA \nYou are the promptest of those who may respond,\nوَ اَكْرَمُ مَنْ عَفٰی \nWA AKRAMO MAN A’FAA \nthe most generous of those who may pardon, \nوَ اَوْسَعُ مَنْ اَعْطٰی \nWA AWSA-O’ MAN A-A’TAA \nthe most liberal of those who give,\nوَ اَسْمَعُ مَنْ سُئِلَ \nWA ASMA-O’ MAN SO-ELA \nand the most responding of those whom are asked.\nیَا رَحْمٰنَ الدُّنْیَا وَ الْاٰخِرَۃِ وَ رَحِیْمَهُمَا \nYAA RAHMAANAD DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE WA RAHEEMAHOMAA \nO All-beneficent of the world and the Hereafter, and All-merciful!\nلَیْسَ كَمِثْلِكَ مَسْئُوْلٌ وَ لَاْ سِوَاكَ مَاْمُوْلٌ \nLAYSA KAMISLEKA MAS-OOLUN WA LAA SEWAAKA MAAMOOLUN \nNo besought one is like You and none save You is hoped.\nدَعَوْتُكَ فَاَجَبْتَنِیْ وَ سَئَلْتُكَ فَاعْطَیْتَنِیْ \nDA-A’WTOKA FA-AJABTANEE WA SA-A’LTOKA FA-A-A’TAYTANEE \nI prayed You and You answered me. I besought You and You gave me.\nوَ رَغِبْتُ اِلَیْكَ فَرَحِمْتَنِیْ وَ وَثِقْتُ بِكَ فَنَجَّیْتَنِیْ \nWA RAGHIBTO ELAYKA FARAHIMTANEE WA WASIQTO BEKA FANAJJAYTANEE \nI desired for You and You had mercy on me. I had confidence in You and You saved me.\nوَ فَزِعْتُ اِلَیْكَ فَكَفَیْتَنِیْ \nWA FAZE’TO ELAYKA FA-KAFAYTANEE \nI resorted to You in awe and You delivered me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA FA-SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad,\nعَبْدِكَ وَ رَسُوْلِكَ وَ نَبِیِّكَ \nA’BDEKA WA ROSOLEKA WA NABIYYEKA \nYour servant, messenger, and prophet,\nوَ عَلٰی اٰلِهِ الطَّیِّبِیْنَ الطَّاهِرِیْنَ اَجْمَعِیْنَ \nWA A’LAA AALEHIT TAYYEBEENAT TAAHEREENA AJMA-E’ENA \nand to all of his Household, the pure and immaculate,\nوَ تَمِّمْ لَنَا نَعْمَآئَكَ وَ هَنِّئْنَا عَطَآئَكَ \nWA TAMMIM LANAA NA’MAAA-AKA WA HANNEA-NAA A’TAAA-AKA \nand perfect for us Your graces, make us taste the pleasure of Your gifts,\nوَ اكْتُبْنَا لَكَ شَاكِرِیْنَ وَ لِاٰلَآئِكَ ذَاكِرِیْنَ \nWAK TUBNAA LAKA SHAAKEREENA WA LE-AALAAA-EKA ZAAKEREENA \nand register us as thankful for You and as oft-referring to You.\nاٰمِیْنَ اٰمِیْنَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِیْنَ اَللّٰهُمَّ یَا مَنْ مَلَكَ فَقَدَرَ \nAAMEENA AAMEENA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA ALLAAHUMMA YAA MAN MALAKA FAQADARA \nRespond, respond! O Lord of the worlds! O Allah, Who owns; therefore, He controls,\nوَ قَدَرَ فَقَهَرَ وَ عُصِیَ فَسَتَرَ \nWA QADARA FAQAHARA WA O’SEYA FASATARA \nand controls; therefore, He has absolute authority, and is disobeyed; yet, He covers,\nوَاسْتُغْفِرَ فَغَفَرَ \nWAS TUGHFERA FA-GHAFARA \nand is prayed for forgiveness; therefore, He forgives.\nیَا غَایَۃَ الطَّالِبِیْنَ الرَّاغِبِیْنَ \nYAA GHAYATAT TAALEBEENAR RAAGHEBEENA \nO He Who is the aim of seekers and desirers\nوَ مُنْتَہٰی اَمَلِ الرَّاجِیْنَ \nWA MUNTAHAA AMALIR RAAJEENA \nand the ultimate purpose of the hope of hopers!\nیَا مَنْ اَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عِلْمًا \nYAA MAN AHAATA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN I’LMAN \nO He Who encompasses all things in knowledge\nوَ وَسِعَ الْمُسْتَقِيْلِیْنَ رَاْفَۃً وَّ رَحْمَۃً وَّحِلْمًا \nWA WASE-A’L MUSTAQBELEENA RAAFATANW WA RAHMATANW WA HILMAN \nand covers those who quit (their sins) with tender, mercy, and forbearance!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا نَتَوَجَّهُ اِلَیْكَ فِیْ ہٰذِهِ الْعَشِیَّۃِ \nALLAAHUMMA INNAA NATAWAJJAHO ELAYKA FEE HAAZEHIL A’SHIYYATIL \nO Allah, we turn our faces to You in this evening\nالَّتِیْ شَرَّفْتَهَا وَ عَظَّمْتَهَا \nLATEE SHARRAFTAHAA WA A’ZZAMTAHAA \nthat You deem honorable and reverential\nبِمُحَمَّدٍ نَبِیِّكَ وَ رَسُوْلِكَ \nBEMOHAMMADIN NABIYYEKA WA RASOOLEKA \n (asking You) in the name of Muhammad, Your Prophet, Messenger,\nوَ خِیَرَتِكَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ وَ اَمِیْنِكَ عَلٰی وَحْیِكَ \nWA KHEYARATEKA MIN KHALQEKA WA AMEENEKA A’LAA WAHYEKAL \nthe best of Your creation, Your trustee on Your Revelation,\nالْبَشِیْرِ النَّذِیْرِ السِّرَاجِ الْمُنِیْرِ \nBASHEERIN NAZEERIS SERAAJIL MONEERIL \nthe bearer of glad tidings, the warner, and the shining lantern,\nالَّذِیْ اَنْعَمْتَ بِہٖ عَلَی الْمُسْلِمِیْنَ \nLAZEE AN-A’MTA BEHI A’LAL MUSLEMEENA \nwith whom You have conferred upon the Muslims,\nوَ جَعَلْتَہٗ رَحْمَۃً لِّلْعَالَمِیْنَ \nWA JA-A’LTAHU RAHMATAN LIL-A’ALAMEENA \nand whom You made mercy for the worlds.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA FASALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nSo, O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nكَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ اَهْلٌ لِذٰلِكَ مِنْكَ یَا عَظِیْمُ \nKAMAA MOHAMMADUN AHLUN LEZAALEKA MINKA YAA A’ZEEMO \nFor as much as Muhammad deserves that from You, O All-great.\nفَصَلِّ عَلَیْهِ وَ عَلٰی اٰلِهِ \nFASALLE A’LAYHE WA A’LAA AALEHIL \nSo, send blessings to him and his Household,\nالْمُنْتَجَبِیْنَ الطَّیِّبِیْنَ الطَّاهِرِیْنَ اَجْمَعِیْنَ \nMUNTAJABEENAT TAYYEBEENAT TAAHEREENA AJMA-E’ENA \nthe elite, pure, and immaculate — all of them,\nوَ تَغَمَّدْنَا بِعَفْوِكَ عَنَّا \nWA TAGHAMMADNAA BE-A’FWEKA A’NNAA \nand encompass us with Your pardoning us.\nفَاِلَیْكَ عَجَّتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ بِصُنُوْفِ اللُّغَاتِ \nFA-ELAYKA AJJATIL ASWAATO BESONOOFIL LOGHAATE \nTo You are the voices of various languages clamoring;\nفَاجْعَلْ لَنَا اَللّٰهُمَّ فِیْ ہٰذِهِ الْعَشِیَّۃِ \nFAJ-A’L LANAA ALLAAHUMMA FEE HAAZEHIL A’SHIYYATE \nso, decide for us, O Allah, in this evening\nنَصِیْبًا مِنْ كُلِّ خَیْرٍ تَقْسِمُہٗ بَیْنَ عِبَادِكَ \nNASEEBAN MIN KULLE KHAYRIN TAQSEMOHU BAYNA E’BAADEKA \na share from every good item that You distribute among Your servants,\nوَ نُوْرٍ تَهْدِیْ بِہٖ وَرَحْمَۃٍ تَنْشُرُهَا \nWA NOORIN TAHDEE BEHI WA RAHMATIN TANSHOROHAA \nillumination by which You guide, mercy that You spread,\nوَ بَرَكَۃٍ تُنْزِلُهَا وَ عَافِیَۃٍ تُجَلِّلُهَا \nWA BARAKATIN TUNZELOHAA WA A’AFEYATIN TOJALLELOHAA \nblessing that You bring down, wellbeing that You extend,\nوَ رِزْقٍ تَبْسُطُہٗ یَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ \nWA RIZQIN TABSOTOHU YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nand sustenance that You stretch, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اقْلِبْنَا فِی ہٰذَا الْوَقْتِ مُنْجِحِیْنَ مُفْلِحِیْنَ \nALLAAHUMMA AQLIBNAA FEE HAAZAL WAQTE MUNJEHEENA MUFLEHEENA \nO Allah, turn us in this hour successful, flourishing,\nمَبْرُوْرِیْنَ غَانِمِیْنَ وَلَاْ تَجْعَلْنَ مِنَ الْقَانِطِیْنَ \nMABROOREENA GHAANEMEENA WA LAA TAJ-A’LNAA MENAL QAANETEENA \nblessed, and gainers. Do not include us with the despondent.\nوَلَاْ تُخْلِنَا مِنْ رَّحْمَتِكَ \nWA LAA TUKHLENAA MIR RAHMATEKA \nDo not leave us without Your mercy.\nوَلَاْ تَحْرِمْنَا مَا نُؤَمِّلُہٗ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ \nWA LAA TAHRIMNAA MAA NOAMMELOHU MIN FAZLEKA \nDo not deprive us of that which we hope from Your favor.\nوَلَاْ تَجْعَلْنَا مِنْ رَّحْمَتِكَ مَحْرُوْمِیْنَ \nWA LAA TAJ-A’LNAA MIR RAHMATEKA MAHROOMEENA \nDo not make us deprived of Your mercy,\nوَلَاْ لِفَضْلِ مَا نُؤَمِّلُہٗ مِنْ عَطَآئِكَ قَانِطِیْنَ \nWA LAA LEFAZLE MAA NOAMMELOHU MIN A’TAAA-EKA QAANETEENA \nor despair of the favor of what we hope from Your gifts.\nوَلَاْ تَرُدَّنَا خَائِبِیْنَ وَلَاْ مِنْۢ بَابِكَ مَطْرُوْدِیْنَ \nWA LAA TARUDDANAA KHAAA-EBEENA WA LAA MIM BAABEKA MATROODEENA \nDo not turns us down disappointed or driven away from Your door.\nیَا اَجْوَدَ اْلَاجْوَدِیْنَ \nYAA AJWADAL AJWADEENA \nO most Magnanimous of all those who treat magnanimously\nوَ اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِیْنَ \nWA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA \nand most Generous of all those who act generously!\nاِلَیْكَ اَقْبَلْنَا مُوْقِنِیْنَ \nELAYKA AQBALNAA MOOQENEENA \nTo You are we advancing with full conviction\nوَ لِبَیْتِكَ الْحَرَامِ اٰمِّیْنَ قَاصِدِیْنَ \nWA LEBAYTEKAL HARAAME AAMMEENA QAASEDEENA \nand to Your Holy House are we betaking ourselves purposefully;\nفَاَعِنَّا عَلٰی مَنَاسِكِنَا وَاَكْمِلْ لَنَا حَجَّنَا \nFA-A-I’NNAA A’LAA MANAASEKENAA WA AKMIL LANAA HAJJANAA \nSo, help us do our rituals (perfectly) perfect for us our pilgrimage\nوَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَعَافِنَا فَقَدْ مَدَدْنَا اِلَیْكَ اَیْدِیَنَا \nWA’ FO A’NNAA WA A’AFENAA FAQAD MADADNAA ELAYKA AYDEYANAA \npardon us, and grant us wellbeing. We are stretching our hands toward You;\nفَهِیَ بِذِلَّۃِ الْاِعْتِرَافِ مَوْسُوْمَۃٌ \nFAHEYA BEZILLATIL E-A’TERAAFE MAWSOOMATUN \nso, they are marked by the humiliation of confession.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاَعْطِنَا فِیْ ہٰذِهِ الْعَشِیَّۃِ مَا سَئَلْنَاكَ \nALLAAHUMMA FA-A-A’TENAA FEE HAAZEHIL A’SHIYYATE MAA SA-ALNAAKA \nO Allah, grant us in this evening that which we have besought from You\nوَاكْفِنَا مَا اسْتَكْفَیْنَا \nWAK FENAA MAS TAKFAYNAA \nand save us from that which we have besought You to save us;\nفَلَاْ كَافِیَ لَنَا سِوَاكَ وَلَاْ رَبَّ لَنَا غَیْرُكَ \nFALAA KAAFEYA LANAA SEWAAKA WA LAA RABBA LANAA GHAYROKA \nfor we have no savior but You and we have no sustainer but You.\nنَافِذٌ فِیْنَا حُكْمُكَ مُحِیْطٌ بِنَا عِلْمُكَ \nNAAFEZUN FEENAA HUKMOKA MOHEETUN BENAA I’LMOKA \nYour decree is prevalent on us, Your knowledge is encompassing us,\nعَدْلٌ فِیْنَا قَضَآؤُكَ اِقْضِ لَنَا الْخَیْرَ \nA’DLUN FEENA QAZAAA-OKA IQZE LANAL KHAYRA \nand Your decisions about us is just. (Please) decree for us that which is good\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْخَیْرِ \nWAJ A’LNAA MIN AHLIL KHAYRE \nand make us of the people of goodness.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ  اَوْجِبْ لَنَا بِجُوْدِكَ عَظِیْمَ الْاَجْرِ \nALLAAHUMMA AWJIB LANAA BEJOODEKA A’ZEEMAL AJRE \nO Allah, decide for us, on account of Your magnanimity, a great reward,\nوَكَرِیْمَ الذُّخْرِ وَ دَوَامَ الْیُسْرِ \nWA KAREEMAZ ZUKHRE WA DAWAAMAL YUSRE \na generous reserve, and a permanent easiness,\nوَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا اَجْمَعِیْنَ وَ لَاْ تُهْلِكْنَا مَعَ الْهَالِكِیْنَ \nWAGH FIR LANAA ZONOOBANAA AJMA-E’ENA WA LAA TOHLIKNAA MA-A’L HAALEKEENA \nand forgive us all our sins, do not annihilate us with those annihilated,\nوَلَاْ تَصْرِفْ عَنَّا رَاْفَتَكَ وَرَحْمَتَكَ \nWA LAA TASRIF A’NNAA RAAFATAKA WA RAHMATAKA \nand do not drive away from us Your tenderness and mercy;\nیَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ \nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنَا فِیْ ہٰذَا الْوَقْتِ مِمَّنْ سَاَلَكَ فَاَعْطَیْتَہٗ \nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNAA FEE HAAZAL WAQTE MIMMAN SA-ALAKA FA-A-A’TAYTAHU \nO Allah, include us, at this hour, with them who besought You and You thus gave them,\nوَشَكَرَكَ فَزِدْتَہٗ \nWA SHAKARAKA FAZIDTAHU \nwho thanked You and You thus increased them,\nوَتَابَ اِلَیْكَ فَقَبِلْتَہٗ \nWA TAABA ELAYKA FAQABILTAHU \nwho returned to You and You thus accepted them,\nوَتَنَصَّلَ اِلَیْكَ مِنْ ذُنُوْبِہٖ كُلِّهَا فَغَفَرْتَهَا لَہٗ \nWA TANASSALA ELAYKA MIN ZONOOBEHI KULLEHAA FAGHAFARTAHAA LAHU \nand who renounced all their sins before You and You thus forgave them;\nیَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ اَللّٰهُمَّ وَنَقِّنَا وَسَدِّدْنَا \nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME ALLAAHUMMA WA WAFFIQNAA WA SADDIDNAA \nO Lord of Majesty and Honor! O Allah, purify us and lead us to success\nوَاقْبَلْ تَضَرُّ عَنَا \nWAQ BAL TAZARRO A’NNAA \nand admit our earnest entreaty;\nیَا خَیْرَ مَنْ سُئِلَ \nYAA KHAYRA MAN SO-ELA \nO He Who is the best of all those who are besought\nوَ یَا اَرْحَمَ مَنِ اسْتُرْحِمَ \nWA YAA ARHAMA MANIS TURHEMA \nand most Merciful of all those whose mercy is sought!\nیَا مَنْ لَاْ یَخْفٰی عَلَیْهِ اِغْمَاضُ الْجُفُوْنِ \nYAA MAN LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYHE IGHMAAZUL JOFOONE \nO He from Whom the closing of eyelids cannot be hidden,\nوَ لَاْ لَحْظُ الْعُیُوْنِ وَ لَاْ مَا اسْتَقَرَّ فِیْ الْمَكْنُوْنِ \nWA LAA LAHZUL O’YOONE WA LAA MAS TAQARRA FIL MAKNOONE \nnor are the glances of eyes, nor is that which settles in the unseen,\nوَ لَاْ مَا انْطَوَتْ عَلَیْهِ مُضْمَرَاتُ الْقُلُوْبِ \nWA LAA MAN TAWAT A’LAYHE MUZMARAATUL QOLOOBE \nnor are things vanished under the secrets of hearts.\nاَلَاْ كُلُّ ذٰلِكَ قَدْ اَحْصَاهُ عِلْمُكَ \nALAA KULLO ZAALEKA QAD AHSAAHO I’LMOKA \nVerily, all that has been encompassed by Your knowledge\nوَ وَسِعَہٗ حِلْمُكَ \nWA WASE-A’HU HILMOKA \nand covered by Your forbearance.\nسُبْحَانَكَ وَتَعَالَیْتَ عَمَّا یَقُوْلُ الظَّلِمُوْنَ \nSUBHAANAKA WA TA-A’ALAYTA A’MMA YAQOOLUZ ZAALEMOONA \nAll glory be to You; and Exalted be You above all that the wrongdoers say,\nعُلُوًّا كَبِیْرًا تُسَبِّحُ لَكَ السَّمٰوٰتُ السَّبْعُ \nO’LUWWAN KABEERAN TOSABBEHO LAKAS SAMAAWAATUS SAB-O’ \nin high exaltation! Declaring You glory are the seven heavens,\nوَالْاَرَضُوْنَ وَ مَنْ فِیْهِنَّ \nWAL ARAZOONA WA MAN FEEHINNA \nthe (layers of the) earth, and all beings therein.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْ شَیْءٍ اِلَّا یُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ \nWA IM MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA YOSABBEHO BEHAMDEKA \nThere is not a thing but celebrates Your praise.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَالْمَجْدُ وَعُلُوُّ الْجَدِّ \nFALAKAL HAMDO WAL MAJDO WA O’LUWWUL JADDE \nYours are all praise, glory, and exaltation of majesty.\nیَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ وَالْفَصْلِ وَالْاِنْعَامِ \nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME WAL FAZLE WAL IN-A’AME \nO Owner of majesty, honor, grace, favoring,\nوَالْاَیَادِی الْجِسَامِ وَ اَنْتَ الْجَوَادُ الْكَرِیْمُ \nWAL AYAADIL JESAAME WA ANTAL JAWAADUL KAREEMUR \nand huge bestowals. You are the All-magnanimous, the All-generous,\nالرَّؤُفُ الرَّحِیْمُ \nRA-OOFUR RAHEEMO \nthe All-tender, the All-merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَوْسِعْ عَلَیَّ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ الْحَلَالِ \nALLAAHUMMA AWSE’ A’LAYYA MIN RIZQEKAL HALAALE \nO Allah, provide me largely with Your legally gotten sustenance,\nوَعَافِنِیْ فِیْ بَدَنِیْ وَدِیْنِیْ \nWA A’AFENEE FEE BADANEE WA DEENEE \ngrant me wellbeing in my body and my faith,\nوَاٰمِنْ خَوْفِیْ وَاَعْتِقْ رَقَبَتِیْ مِنَ النَّارِ \nWA AAMIN KHAWFEE WA A-A’TIQ RAQABATEE MENAN NAARE \nsecure my fears, and release me from Hellfire.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَاْ تَمْكُرْ بِیْ وَ لَاْ تَسْتَدْرِجْنِیْ \nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAMKUR BEE WA LAA TASTADRIJNEE \nO Allah, do not plan against me, do not draw me near to destruction,\nوَ لَاْ تَخْدَعْنِیْ \nWA LAA TAKH-DA’NEE \ndo not overreach me,\nوَادْرَأْ عَنِّیْ شَرَّ فَسَقَۃِ الْجِنِّ وَاْلاِنْسِ.\nWAD RAA A’NNEE SHARRA FASAQATIL JINNE WAL INSE.\nand drive away from me the evils of the corruptive Jinn and men.\nImam al-Husain (a.s.) then raised his head and sight to the sky with teary eyes and said with an audible voice:\nیَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِیْنَ \nYAA ASMA-A’S SAAME-E’ENA \nO most Hearing of all those who can hear! \nیَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِیْنَ \nYAA ABSARAN NAAZEREENA \nO most Seeing of all those who can see!\nوَ یَا اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِیْنَ \nYAA ASRA-A’L HAASEBEENA \nAnd O swiftest of all those who call to account! \nوَ یَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ \nWA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nAnd O most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nصَلِّ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADENIS \nsend blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nالسَّادَۃِ الْمَیَامِیْنَ وَ اَسْئَلُكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ حَاجَتِیَ \nSAADATIL MAYAAMEENA WA AS-ALOKA ALLAAHUMMA HAAJATEYAL \nthe auspicious chiefs; and I beseech You for my request\nالَّتِیْ اِنْ اَعْطَیْتَنِیْهَا لَمْ یَضُرَّنِیْ مَا مَنَعْتَنِیْ \nLATEE IN A-A’TAYTANEEHAA LAM YAZURRANEE MAA MANA’-TANEE \nthat if You answer, anything else that You reject will not harm me\nوَاِنْ مَنَعْتَنِيْهَا لَمْ یَنْفَعُنِیْ مَا اَعْطَیْنَتِیْ \nWA IN MANA’TANEEHAA LAM YANFA-O’NEE MAA A-A’TAYTANEE \nand if You reject, anything else that You respond will not benefit me.\nاَسْئَلُكَ فَكَاكَ رَقَبَتِیْ مِنَ النَّارِ لَاْ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nAS-ALOKA FAKAAKA RAQABATEE MENAN NAARE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA \nI beseech You for releasing me from Hellfire. There is no god save You,\nوَحْدَكَ لَاْ شَرِیْكَ لَكَ لَكَ الْمُلْكُ وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ \nWAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAKA LAKAL MULKO WA LAKAL HAMDO \nonly You, there is no partner with You. To You is the kingdom and to You is all praise,\nوَ اَنْتَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nWA ANTA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nand You have power over all things. \nیَا رَبِّ یَا رَبِّ یَا رَبِّ...\nYAA RABBE YAA RABBE YAA RABBE.\nO my Lord! O my Lord! O my Lord…\nImam al-Husain (a.s.) then repeated yaa-rabbe so frequently and effectively that he attracted the attentions of all the others who, instead of praying for granting their needs, surrounded Imam al-Husain (a.s.) to listen to him and pray for the response of his supplication. Then, they wept with him. At sunset, they left Mount Arafaat with him.\nThis is the end of Imam al-Husain (a.s.)’s supplicatory prayer on the Arafat Day according to the narrations of al-Kafami in his book of al-Balad al-Ameen and Allamah al-Majlisi in his book of Zaad al-Maad. As for Sayyid Ibn Taaoos, he, in his book of Iqbal al-Aamaal, adds the following statements to the supplicatory prayer:\nاِلٰهِيْ اَنَا الْفَقِيْرُ فِيْ غِنَايَ \nELAAHEE ANAL FAQEERO FEE GHENAAYA \nO my God, I am needy despite my richness; \nفَكَيْفَ لَاْ اَكُوْنُ فَقِيْرًا فِيْ فَقْرِيْ؟\nFAKAYFA LAA AKOONO FAQEERAN FEE FAQREE? \nso, how can I not be needy in my neediness?\nاِلٰهِيْ اَنَا الْجَاهِلُ فِيْ عِلْمِيْ\nELAAHEE ANAL JAAHELO FEE I’LMEE \nO my God, I am ignorant despite my knowledge;\nفَكَيْفَ لَاْ اَكُوْنُ جَهُوْلًا فِيْ جَهْلِيْ؟\nFAKAYFA LAA AKOONO JAHOOLAN FEE JAHLEE? \nso, how can I not be ignorant in my ignorance?\nاِلٰهِيْ اِنَّ اخْتِلَافَ تَدْبِيْرِكَ\nELAAHEE INNAKH TELAAFA TADBEEREKA \nO my God, the variety of Your regulating of matters\nوَسُرْعَةَ طَوَاءِ مَقَادِيْرِكَ\nWA SUR-A’TA TAWAAA-E MAQAADEEREKA \nand the swiftness of changes in Your ordainments\nمَنَعَا عِبَادَكَ الْعَارِفِيْنَ بِكَ عَنِ السُّكُوْنِ اِلٰى عَطَاءٍ\nMANA-A’A E’BAADAKAL A’AREFEENA BEKA A’NIS SOKOONE ELAA A’TAAA-IN \nhave urged Your servants, who recognize You, not to stop at a certain gift\nوَالْيَاسِ مِنْكَ فِيْ بَلَاءٍ\nWAL YAASE MINKA FEE BALAAA-IN \nand not to despair of You in tribulations.\nاِلٰهِيْ مِنِّيْ مَا يَلِيْقُ بِلُؤْمِيْ\nELAAHI MINNEE MAA YALEEQO BE-LOAMEE \nO my God, coming out of me is that which fits my lowliness;\nوَمِنْكَ مَا يَلِيْقُ بِكَرَمِكَ\nWA MINKA MAA YALEEQO BEKARAMEKA \nbut coming from You is that which befits Your nobleness.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَصَفْتَ نَفْسَكَ بِاللُّطْفِ وَالرَّافَةِ لِيْ\nELAAHEE WASAFTA NAFSAKA BIL-LUTFE WAR-RAAFATE LEE \nO my God, You had ascribed to Yourself gentleness and kindness to me\nقَبْلَ وُجُوْدِ ضَعْفِيْ\nQABLA WOJOODE ZA’FEE \nbefore the existence of my weakness.\nاَفَتَمْنَعُنِيْ مِنْهُمَا بَعْدَ وُجُوْدِ ضَعْفِيْ؟\nAFATAMNA-O’NEE MINHOMAA BA’DA WOJOODE ZA’FEE? \nWill You deprive me of these two after the emergence of my weakness?\nاِلٰهِيْ اِنْ ظَهَرَتِ الْمَحَاسِنُ مِنِّيْ\nELAAHEE IN ZAHARATIL MAHAASENO MINNEE \nO my God, if amenities appear in my conduct,\nفَبِفَضْلِكَ وَلَكَ الْمِنَّةُ عَلَيَّ\nFABE-FAZLEKA WA LAKAL MINNATO A’LAYYA \nthen that is on account of Your favors and Your conferral on me.\nوَاِنْ ظَهَرَتِ الْمَسَاوِىْ مِنِّيْ\nWA IN ZAHARATIL MOSAAWEE MINNEE \nIf evildoings appear in my conduct,\nفَبِعَدْلِكَ وَلَكَ الْحُجَّةُ عَلَيَّ\nFABE-A’DLEKA WA LAKAL HUJJATO A’LAYYA \nthen that is still Your justice and You have claim against me.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ تَكِلُنِيْ وَقَدْ تَكَفَّلْتَ لِيْ؟\nELAAHEE KAYFA TAKELONEE WA QAD TAKAFFALTA LEE? \nO my God, how may it be that You abandon me after You have vouched for me?\nوَكَيْفَ اَضَامُ وَاَنْتَ النَّاصِرُ لِيْ؟\nWA KAYFA AZAAMO WA ANTAN NAASERO LEE? \nHow may I be aggrieved and You are my support?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اَخِيْبُ وَاَنْتَ الْحَفِيُّ بِيْ؟\nAM KAYFA AKHEEBO WA ANTAL HAFIYYO BEE? \nHow may I be disappointed and You are undertaking my affairs?\nهَا اَنَا اَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ بِفَقْرِيْ اِلَيْكَ\nHAA ANAA ATAWASSALO ELAYKA BE-FAQREE ELAYKA \nHere I am begging You by my need for You.\nوَكَيْفَ اَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ بِمَا هُوَ مَحَالٌ اَنْ يَصِلَ اِلَيْكَ؟\nWA KAYFA ATAWASSALO ELAYKA BEMAA HOWA MAHAALUN AN YASELA ELAYKA? \nHow can I beg You by something that is impossible to reach You?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اَشْكُوْ اِلَيْكَ حَالِيْ وَهُوَ لَاْ يَخْفٰى عَلَيْكَ؟\nAM KAYFA ASHKOO ELAYKA HAALEE WA HOWA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYKA? \nHow can I complain to You about my manners while they cannot be hidden from You?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اُتَرْجِمُ بِمَقَالِيْ وَهُوَ مِنْكَ بَرَزٌ اِلَيْكَ؟\nAM KAYFA OTARJEMO BEMAQAALEE WA HOWA MINKA BARAZUN ELAYKA? \nHow can I interpret my words while You are their source?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ تُخَيِّبُ آمَالِيْ وَهِيَ قَدْ وَفَدَتْ اِلَيْكَ؟\nAM KAYFA TOKHAYYEBO AAMAALEE WA HEYA QAD WAFA-DAT ELAYKA? \nHow come that You may let down my hopes, while they are addressed to You?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ لَاْ تُحْسِنُ اَحْوَالِيْ وَبِكَ قَامَتْ\nAM KAYFA LAA TOHSENO AHWAALEE WA BEKA QAAMAT \nHow come that You may not improve my conditions while they are originated by You?\nاِلٰهِيْ مَا اَلْطَفَكَ بِيْ مَعَ عَظِيْمِ جَهْلِيْ\nELAAHEE MAA ALTAFAKA BEE MA-A’ A’ZEEME JAHLEE \nO my God, how gentle You are to me despite my notorious ignorance!\nوَمَا اَرْحَمَكَ بِيْ مَعَ قَبِيْحِ فِعْلِيْ\nWA MAA ARHAMAKA BEE MA-A’ QABEEHE FE’LEE \nHow merciful You are to me despite my hideous deeds!\nاِلٰهِيْ مَا اَقْرَبَكَ مِنِّيْ وَاَبْعَدَنِيْ عَنْكَ\nELAAHEE MAA AQRABAKA MINNEE WA AB-A’DANEE A’NKA \nO my God, how nigh to me You are and how far from You I am!\nوَمَا اَرْاَفَكَ بِيْ فَمَا الَّذِيْ يَحْجُبُنِيْ عَنْكَ؟\nWA MAA AR-AFAKA BEE FAMAL LAZEE YAHJOBONEE A’NKA? \nHow kind to me You are; so, what is that which can prevent me from You?\nاِلٰهِيْ عَلِمْتُ بِاخْتِلَافِ الْآثَارِوَتَنَقُّلَاتِ الْاَطْوَارِ\nELAAHEE A’LIMTO BIKHTELAAFIL AASAARE WA TANAQQOLAATIL ATWAARE \nO my God, I have known, through variety of signs and changes of phases,\nاَنَّ مُرَادَكَ مِنِّيْ اَنْ تَتَعَرَّفَ اِلَيَّ فِيْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nANNA MORAADAKA MINNEE AN TATA-A’RRAFA ELAYYA FEE KULLE SHAY-IN \nthat what You want from me is that You introduce Yourself to me in all things\nحَتّٰى لَاْ اَجْهَلَكَ فِيْ شَيْءٍ\nHATTAA LAA AJ-HALAKA FEE SHAY-IN \nso that I will not ignore You in any thing.\nاِلٰهِيْ كُلَّمَا اَخْرَسَنِيْ لُؤْمِيْ\nELAAHEE KULLAMAA AKRASANEE LOA-MEE \nO my God, whenever my lowliness suppresses my voice,\nاَنْطَقَنِيْ كَرَمُكَ\nANTAQANEE KARAMOKA \nYour nobility encourages me to speak.\nوَكُلَّمَا آيَسَتْنِيْ اَوْصَافِيْ اَطْمَعَتْنِيْ مِنَنُكَ\nWA KULLAMAA AAYASATNEE AWSAAFEE AT-MA-A’TNEE MENANOKA \nWhenever my features lead me to despair (of You), Your bestowals make me crave for You.\nاِلٰهِيْ مَنْ كَانَتْ مَحَاسِنُهٗ مَسَاوِىَ\nELAAHEE MAN KAANAT MAHAASENOHU MASAAWE-YA \nO my God, as for he whose good deeds are wrongdoings;\nفَكَيْفَ لَاْ تَكُوْنُ مَسَاوِئُهٗ مَسَاوِىَ؟\nFAKAYFA LAA TAKOONO MASAAWEEHE MASAAWEYA? \nhow can his wrongdoings not be wrongdoings?\nوَمَنْ كَانَتْ حَقَائِقُهٗ دَعَاوِيَ\nWA MAN KAANAT HAQAA-EQOHU DA-A’AWEYA \nAs for he whose facts are mere claims,\nفَكَيْفَ لَاْ تَكُوْنُ دَعَاوَاهُ دَعَاوِيَ؟\nFA-KAYFA LAA TAKOONO DA-A’AWEEHE DA-A’AWEYA? \nhow can his claims not be claims?\nاِلٰهِيْ حُكْمُكَ النَّافِذُ وَمَشِيْئَتُكَ الْقَاهِرَةُ\nELAAHEE HUKMOKAN NAAFEZO WA MASHIYYATOKAL QAAHERATO \nO my God, Your unstoppable decree and Your surmounting volition\nلَمْ يَتْرُكَا لِذِيْ مَقَالٍ مَقَالًا\nLAM YATROKAA LE-ZEE MAQAALIN MAQAALAN \nhave not left any word to be said by any orator\nوَلَاْ لِذِيْ حَالٍ حَالًا\nWA LAA LE ZEE HAALIN HAALAN \nand have not left any manner to be displayed.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَمْ مِنْ طَاعَةٍ بَنَيْتُهَا\nELAAHEE KAM MIN TAA-A’TIN BANAYTOHAA \nO my God, too many are the acts of obedience that I have prepared\nوَحَالَةٍ شَيَّدْتُهَا\nWA HAALATIN SHAYYAD-TOHA \nand the conducts that I have established,\nهَدَمَ اعْتِمَادِيْ عَلَيْهَا عَدْلُكَ\nHADAMA’ TEMAADEE A’LAYHAA A’DLOKA \nbut Your justice has ruined my reliance on these,\nبَلْ اَقَالَنِيْ مِنْهَا فَضْلُكَ\nBAL AQAALANEE MINHAA FAZLOKA \nand, moreover, Your favoring has made me abandon them.\nاِلٰهِيْ اِنَّكَ تَعْلَمُ\nELAAHEE INNAKA TA’LAMO \nO my God, You surely know\nاَنِّيْ وَاِنْ لَّمْ تَدُمِ الطَّاعَةُ مِنِّيْ فِعْلًا جَزْمًا\nANNEE WA IL LAM TADOMIT TAA-A’TO MINNEE FE’LAN JAZMAN \nthat even my obedience (to You) has not lasted in reality,\nفَقَدْ دَامَتْ مَحَبَّةً وَعَزْمًا\nFAQAD DAAMAT MAHABBATAN WA A’ZMAN \nit has lasted in love (for it) and determination (to do it)!\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اَعْزِمُ وَاَنْتَ الْقَاهِرُ؟\nELAAHEE KAYFA A-A’ZEMO WA ANTAL QAAHERO? \nO my God, how can I determine, while You are All-supreme?\nوَكَيْفَ لَاْ اَعْزِمُ وَاَنْتَ الْآمِرُ؟\nWA KAYFA LAA A-A’ZEMO WA ANTAL AAMERO? \nHow can I quit determining, while it is Your command (to determine)?\nاِلٰهِيْ تَرَدُّدِيْ فِيْ الْآثَارِيُوْجِبُ بُعْدَ الْمَزَارِ\nELAAHEE TARADDODEE FIL AASAARE YOOJEBO BOA’DAL MAZAARE \nO my God, my hesitation in (following) Your traces will result in unlikely visitation;\nفَاجْمَعْنِيْ عَلَيْكَ بِخِدْمَةٍ تُوْصِلُنِيْ اِلَيْكَ\nFAJ-MA’NEE A’LAYKA BEKHIDMATIN TOOSELONEE ELAYKA \nso, join me to You through a service that takes me to You.\nكَيْفَ يُسْتَدَلُّ عَلَيْكَ بِمَا هُوَ فِيْ وُجُوْدِهٖ مُفْتَقِرٌ اِلَيْكَ؟\nKAYFA YUSTADALLO A’LAYKA BEMAA HOWA FEE WOJOODEHEE MUFTAQERUN ELAYKA?\nHow can You be figured out through that whose existence relies on You?\nاَيَكُوْنُ لِغَيْرِكَ مِنَ الظُّهُوْرِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ\nA-YAKOONO LEGHAYREKA MENAZ ZOHOORE MAA LAYSA LAKA \nCan any thing other than You hold a (kind of) manifestation that You lack\nحَتّٰى يَكُوْنَ هُوَ الْمُظْهِرَ لَكَ؟\nHATTAA YAKOONA HOWAL MUZHERA LAKA? \nand thus it may act as an appearance for You?\nمَتٰى غِبْتَ حَتّٰى تَحْتَاجَ اِلٰى دَلِيْلٍ يَدُلُّ عَلَيْكَ؟\nMATAA GHIBTA HATTAA TAHTAAJA ELAA DALEELIN YADULLO A’LAYKA? \nWhen have You ever been absent so that You may need something to point to You?\nوَمَتٰى بَعُدْتَ حَتّٰى تَكُوْنَ الْآثَارُ هِيَ الَّتِيْ تُوْصِلُ اِلَيْكَ؟\nWA MATAA BA-U’DTA HATTAA TAKOONAL AASAARO HEYAL LATEE TOOSELO ELAYKA? \nWhen have You ever been far-off so that traces may lead to You?\nعَمِيَتْ عَيْنٌ لَاْ تَرَاكَ عَلَيْهَا رَقِيْبًا\nA’MEYAT A’YNUN LAA TARAAKA A’LAYHAA RAQEEBAN \nBlind be the eye that cannot see You watching it.\nوَخَسِرَتْ صَفْقَةُ عَبْدٍ لَمْ تَجْعَلْ لَهٗ مِنْ حُبِّكَ نَصِيْبًا\nWA KHASERAT SAFQATO A’BDIN LAM TAJ-A’L LAHU MIN HUBBEKA NASEEBAN \nLosing is a servant’s deal that does not dedicate a share to the love for You.\nاِلٰهِيْ اَمَرْتَ بِالرُّجُوْعِ اِلَى الْآثَارِ\nELAAHEE AMARTA BIR-ROJOO-E’ ELAL AASAARE \nO my God, You have ordered us to refer to the traces;\nفَارْجِعْنِيْ اِلَيْكَ بِكِسْوَةِ الْاَنْوَارِ\nFAR-JE’NEE ELAYKA BEKISWATIL ANWAARE \ntherefore, (please do) make me refer to You with the garb of lights\nوَهِدَايَةِ الْاِسْتِبْصَارِ\nWA HEDAAYATIL ISTIBSAARE \nand the guidance of insight\nحَتّٰى اَرْجِعَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهَا كَمَا دَخَلْتُ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهَا\nHATTAA AR-JE-A’ ELAYKA MINHAA KAMAA DAKHALTO ELAYKA MINHAA \nso that I will return to You in the same way as I have entered to You from them\nمَصُوْنَ السِّرِّ عَنِ النَّظَرِ اِلَيْهَا\nMASOONAS SIRRE A’NIN NAZARE ELAYHAA \nas being too protected to look at them\nوَمَرْفُوْعَ الْهِمَّةِ عَنِ الْاِعْتِمَادِ عَلَيْهَا\nWA MARFOO-I’L HIMMATE A’NIL E-A’TEMAADE A’LAYHAA \nand too determining to depend upon them,\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nfor You have power over all things.\nاِلٰهِيْ هٰذَا ذُلِّيْ ظَاهِرٌ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nELAAHEE HAAZAA ZULLEE ZAAHERUN BAYNA YADAYKA \nO my God, this is my humiliation; it manifests itself before You.\nوَهٰذَا حَالِيْ لَاْ يَخْفٰى عَلَيْكَ\nWA HAAZAA HAALEE LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYKA \nThis is my manner; it cannot be concealed against You.\nمِنْكَ اَطْلُبُ الْوُصُوْلَ اِلَيْكَ\nMINKA ATLOBUL WOSOOLA ELAYKA \nFrom You do I beseech soaring to You\nوَبِكَ اَسْتَدِلُّ عَلَيْكَ\nWA BEKA ASTADILLO A’LAYKA \nand through You do I take the way to You.\nفَاهْدِنِيْ بِنُوْرِكَ اِلَيْكَ\nFAH-DENEE BENOOREKA ELAYKA \nSo, (please do) guide me to You through Your Light\nوَاَقِمْنِيْ بِصِدْقِ الْعُبُوْدِيَّةِ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWA AQIMNEE BESIDQIL O’BOODIYYATE BAYNA YADAYKA \nand make me stand up before Your Hands with the true servitude to You.\nاِلٰهِيْ عَلِّمْنِيْ مِنْ عِلْمِكَ الْمَخْزُوْنِ\nELAAHEE A’LLIMNEE MIN I’LMEKAL MAKHZOONE \nO my God, teach me from Your veiled knowledge\nوَصُنِّيْ بِسِتْرِكَ الْمَصُوْنِ\nWA SUNNEE BESITREKAL MASOONE \nand protect me with Your shielding shelter.\nاِلٰهِيْ حَقِّقْنِيْ بِحَقَائِقِ اَهْلِ الْقُرْبِ\nELAAHEE HAQQIQNEE BE-HAQAAA-EKE AHLIL QURBE \nO my God, (please do) grant me the realities that are enjoyed by the people who are near to You\nوَاسْلُكْ بِيْ مَسْلَكَ اَهْلِ الْجَذْبِ\nWAS LUK BEE MAS-LAKA AHLIL JAZBE \nand make me follow the course of the people who are attracted to You.\nاِلٰهِيْ اَغْنِنِيْ بِتَدْبِيْرِكَ لِيْ عَنْ تَدْبِيْرِيْ\nELAAHEE AGHNENEE BE-TADBEEREKA LEE A’N TADBEEREE \nO my God, make Your management of my affairs replace my management of my affairs,\nوَبِاخْتِيَارِكَ عَنِ اخْتِيَارِيْ\nWA BIKH-TEYAAREKA A’NIKH TEYAAREE \nmake Your choice for me replace my choice for myself,\nوَاَوْقِفْنِيْ عَلٰى مَرَاكِزِ اضْطِرَارِيْ\nWA AWQIFNEE A’LAA MARAAKEZIZ TERAAREE \nand make me stop at the points of emergency.\nاِلٰهِيْ اَخْرِجْنِيْ مِنْ ذُلِّ نَفْسِيْ\nELAAHEE AKHRIJNEE MIN ZULLE NAFSEE \nO my God, (please do) take my out of the humiliation of myself\nوَطَهِّرْنِيْ مِنْ شَكِّيْ وَشِرْكِيْ قَبْلَ حُلُوْلِ رَمْسِيْ\nWA TAHHIRNEE MIN SHAKKEE WA SHIRKEE QABLA HOLOOLE RAMSEE \nand purify me from my suspicion and polytheism before I enter my grave.\nبِكَ اَنْتَصِرُ فَانْصُرْنِيْ\nBEKA ANTASERO FAN-SURNEE \nOnly through You do I achieve victory; so, (please do) give me victory.\nوَعَلَيْكَ اَتَوَكَّلُ فَلَاْ تَكِلْنِيْ\nWA A’LAYKA ATAWAKKALO FALAA TAKILNEE \nOnly upon You do I rely; so, do not refer me to anyone else.\nوَاِيَّاكَ اَسْاَلُ فَلَاْ تُخَيِّبْنِيْ\nWA IYYAAKA AS-ALO FALAA TOKHAYYIBNEE \nOnly You do I beseech; so, do not disappoint me.\nوَفِيْ فَضْلِكَ اَرْغَبُ فَلَاْ تَحْرِمْنِيْ\nWA FEE FAZLEKA ARGHABO FALAA TAHRIMNEE \nOnly for Your favors do I desire; so, do not deprive me (of Your favors).\nوَبِجَنَابِكَ اَنْتَسِبُ فَلَاْ تُبْعِدْنِيْ\nWA BEJANAABEKA ANTASEBO FALAA TUB-I’DNEE \nOnly to Your side do I resort; so, do not set me aside.\nوَبِبَابِكَ اَقِفُ فَلَاْ تَطْرُدْنِيْ\nWA BE-BAABEKA AQEFO FALAA TATRUDNEE \nAt Your door only do I stand; so, do not drive me away.\nاِلٰهِيْ تَقَدَّسَ رِضَاكَ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ لَهٗ عِلَّةٌ مِنْكَ\nELAAHEE TAQADDASA REZAAKA AN-Y YAKOONA LAHU I’LLATUN MINKA \nO my God, Your pleasure is too sanctified to receive a defect from You;\nفَكَيْفَ يَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عِلَّةٌ مِنِّيْ؟\nFA-KAYFA YAKOONO I’LLATUN MINNEE? \nhence, how can it receive a defect from me?\nاِلٰهِيْ اَنْتَ الْغَنِيُّ بِذَاتِكَ اَنْ يَّصِلَ اِلَيْكَ النَّفْعُ مِنْكَ\nELAAHEE ANTAL GHANIYYO BEZAATEKA AN-Y YASELA ELAYKAN NAF-O’ MINKA \nO my God, You are too self-sufficient by Yourself to be benefited by Yourself;\nفَكَيْفَ لَاْ تَكُوْنُ غَنِيًّا عَنِّيْ؟\nFAKAYA LAA TAKOONO GHANIYYAN A’NNEE? \nhence, how can You not be self-sufficient from me?\nاِلٰهِيْ اِنَّ الْقَضَاءَ وَالْقَدَرَ يُمَنِّيْنِيْ\nELAAHEE INNAL QAZAAA-A WAL QADARE YOMANNEENEE \nO my God, fate awakens my hope\nوَاِنَّ الْهَوٰى بِوَثَآئِقِ الشَّهْوَةِ اَسَرَنِيْ\nWA INNAL HAWAA BEWASAAA-EQISH SHAH-WATE ASARANEE \nand whim has enchained me with the firm chains of lust;\nفَكُنْ اَنْتَ النَّصِيْرَ لِيْ حَتّٰى تَنْصُرَنِيْ وَتُبَصِّرَنِيْ\nFAKUN ANTAN NASEERA LEE HATTAA TANSORANEE WA TOBASSERANEE \nso, (please do) be my Supporter so that You shall back me and show me the right path.\nوَاَغْنِنِيْ بِفَضْلِكَ\nWA AGHNENEE BEFAZLEKA \nAnd (please do) help me (to dispense with anyone else) through Your favors\nحَتّٰى اَسْتَغْنِيَ بِكَ عَنْ طَلَبِيْ\nHATTAA ASTAGHNEYA BEKA A’N TALABEE \nso that I shall depend upon You exclusively in my requests.\nاَنْتَ الَّذِي اَشْرَقْتَ الْاَنْوَارَ فِيْ قُلُوْبِ اَوْلِيَائِكَ\nANTAL LAZEE ASHRAQTAL ANWAARA FEE QOLOOBE AWLEYAAA-EKA \nIt is You Who have lit the illuminations in the hearts of Your intimate servants\nحَتّٰى عَرَفُوْكَ وَوَحَّدُوْكَ\nHATTAA A’R-AFOOKA WA WAHHADOOKA \nso that they have recognized and testified Your Oneness.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اَزَلْتَ الْاَغْيَارَ عَنْ قُلُوْبِ اَحِبَّائِكَ\nWA ANTAL LAZEE AZALTAL AGHYAARA A’N QOLOOBE AHIBBAAA-EKA \nIt is You Who have removed love for others from the hearts of Your lovers\nحَتّٰى لَمْ يُحِبُّوْا سِوَاكَ وَلَمْ يَلْجَأُوْا اِلٰى غَيْرِكَ\nHATTAA LAM YOHIBBOO SEWAAKA WA LAM YAL-JA-OO ELAA GHAYREKA \nso that they have loved none save You and they have resorted to none save You.\nاَنْتَ الْمُؤْنِسُ لَهُمْ حَيْثُ اَوْحَشَتْهُمُ الْعَوَالِمُ\nANTAL MOONESO LAHUM HAYSO AW HASHAT-HOMUL A’WAALEMO \nYou alone are entertaining them when they have felt lonely because of the other worlds.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ هَدَيْتَهُمْ حَيْثُ اسْتَبَانَتْ لَهُمُ الْمَعَالِمُ\nWA ANTAL LAZEE HADAYTAHUM HAYSUS TABAANAT LAHOMUL MA-A’ALEMO \nYou alone have guided them so that all other worlds manifested themselves before them.\nمَاذَا وَجَدَ مَنْ فَقَدَكَ؟\nMAA ZAA WAJADA MAN FAQADAKA? \nWhat can one who misses You find any substitute?\nوَمَا الَّذِيْ فَقَدَ مَنْ وَجَدَكَ؟\nWA MAL LAZEE FAQADA MAN WAJADAKA? \nWhat can one who finds You miss anything else?\nلَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ رَضِيَ دُوْنَكَ بَدَلًا\nLAQAD KHAABA MAN RAZEYA DOONAKA BADALAN \nDefinitely, failing is he who has accepted anyone other than You as substitute.\nوَلَقَدْ خَسِرَ مَنْ بَغٰى عَنْكَ مُتَحَوِّلًا\nWA LAQAD KHASERA MAN BAGHAA A’NKA MOTAHAWWELAN \nDefinitely, loser is he who have desired for anyone other than You.\nكَيْفَ يُرْجٰى سِوَاكَ\nKAYFA YURJAA SEWAAKA \nHow can anyone other than You be hoped\nوَاَنْتَ مَا قَطَعْتَ الْاِحْسَانَ؟\nWA ANTA MAA QATA’TAL EHSAANA? \nwhilst You have never stopped Your bounties?\nوَكَيْفَ يُطْلَبُ مِنْ غَيْرِكَ\nWA KAYFA YUTLABO MIN GHAYREKA \nHow can anyone other than You be besought\nوَاَنْتَ مَا بَدَّلْتَ عَادَةَ الْاِمْتِنَانِ؟\nWA ANTA MAA BADDALTA A’ADATAL IMTENAANE? \nwhilst You have never changed Your habit of ceaseless bestowal?\nيَا مَنْ اَذَاقَ اَحِبَّائَهٗ حَلَاوَةَ الْمُؤَانَسَةِ\nYAA MAN A-ZAAQA AHIBBAAA-AHU HALAAWATAL MOAANASATE \nO He Who has made His lovers the sweet taste of entertainment;\nفَقَامُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مُتَمَلِّقِيْنَ\nFAQAMOO BAYNA YADAYHE MOTAMALLEQEENA \ntherefore, they have stood up before Him flattering Him!\nوَيَا مَنْ اَلْبَسَ اَوْلِيَآءَهُ مَلَابِسَ هَيْبَتِهٖ\nWA YAA MAN ALBASA AWLEYAAA-AHU MALAABESA HAYBATEHI \nO He Who has dressed His intimate servants the garments of fearing Him;\nفَقَامُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مُسْتَغْفِرِيْنَ\nFAQAAMOO BAYNA YADAYHE MUSTAGHFEREENA \ntherefore, they have stood before Him seeking His forgiveness!\nاَنْتَ الذَّاكِرُ قَبْلَ الذَّاكِرِيْنَ\nANTAZ ZAAKERO QABLAZ ZAAKEREENA \nYou do mention the others (with bounties) before they mention You.\nوَاَنْتَ الْبَادِئُ بِالْاِحْسَانِ قَبْلَ تَوَجُّهِ الْعَابِدِيْنَ\nWA ANTAL BAADEE BIL-EHSAANE QABLA TAWAJJOHIL A’ABEDEENA \nYou do spread Your compassion before the worshippers direct towards You.\nوَاَنْتَ الْجَوَادُ بِالْعَطَاءِ قَبْلَ طَلَبِ الطَّالِبِيْنَ\nWA ANTAL JAWAADO BIL-A’TAA-E QABLA TALABIT TAALEBEENA \nYou do give generously before You are asked.\nوَاَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ ثُمَّ لِمَا وَهَبْتَ لَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْتَقْرِضِيْنَ\nWA ANTAL WAHHAABO SUMMA LEMAA WAHABTA LANAA MENAL MUSTAQREZEENA \nYou do bestow upon us and then borrow from us that which You have bestowed upon us.\nاِلٰهِيْ اُطْلُبْنِيْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ حَتّٰى اَصِلَ اِلَيْكَ\nELAAHEE UTLUBNEE BE-RAHMATEKA HATTAA A-SELA ELAYKA \nO my God, (please do) refer to me with Your mercy so that I will appear before You.\nوَاجْذِبْنِيْ بِمَنِّكَ حَتّٰى اُقْبِلَ عَلَيْكَ\nWAJ ZIBNEE BEMANNEKA HATTAA UQBELA A’LAYKA \n draw me towards You through Your endless favoring so that I will advance to You.\nاِلٰهِيْ اِنَّ رَجَائِي لَاْ يَنْقَطِعُ عَنْكَ وَاِنْ عَصَيْتُكَ\nELAAHEE INNA RAJAAA-EE LAA YANQATE-O’ A’NKA WA IN A’SAYTOKA \nO my God, verily, my hope for You does not cease despite that I may disobey You.\nكَمَا اَنَّ خَوْفِيْ لَاْ يُزَايِلُنِيْ وَاِنْ اَطَعْتُكَ\nKAMAA ANNA KHAWFEE LAA YOZAAYELONEE WA IN A-TA’TOKA \nSimilarly, my fear from You does not leave me even if I obey You.\nفَقَدْ دَفَعَتْنِيَ الْعَوَالِمُ اِلَيْكَ\nFAQAD DA-FA-A’TNIL A’WAALEMO ELAYKA \nThe Worlds have pushed me towards You\nوَقَدْ اَوْقَعَنِيْ عِلْمِيْ بِكَرَمِكَ عَلَيْكَ\nWA QAD AWQA-A’NEE I’LMEE BEKARAMEKA A’LAYKA \nand my acquaintance with Your magnanimity has led me to You.\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اَخِيْبُ وَاَنْتَ اَمَلِيْ؟\nELAAHEE KAYFA AKHEEBO WA ANTA AMALEE? \nO my God, how can I fail whilst You are my hope?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اُهَانُ وَعَلَيْكَ مُتَّكَلِيْ؟\nAM KAYFA OHAANO WA A’LAYKA MUTTAKALEE? \nHow can I be humiliated whilst I depend upon You?\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اَسْتَعِزُّ وَفِيْ الذِّلَّةِ اَرْكَزْتَنِيْ؟\nELAAHEE KAYFA ASTA-I’ZZO WA FIZ ZILLATE ARKAZTANEE? \nHow can see dignity if You fix me in humiliation?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ لَاْ اَسْتَعِزُّ وَاِلَيْكَ نَسَبْتَنِيْ؟\nAM KAYFA LAA AS-TAI’ZZO WA ELAYKA NASABTANEE? \nHow can I not see dignity whilst You have referred me to You?\nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ لَاْ اَفْتَقِرُ وَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ فِيْ الْفُقَرَاءِ اَقَمْتَنِيْ؟\nELAAHEE KAYFA LAA AFTAQERO WA ANTAL LAZEE FIL FOQARAAA-E AQAMTANEE? \nO my God, how can I not be needy whilst it is You Who have lodged me among the needy?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ اَفْتَقِرُ وَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ بِجُوْدِكَ اَغْنَيْتَنِيْ؟\nAM KAYFA AFTAQERO WA ANTAL LAZEE BEJOODEKA AGHNAYTANEE? \nHow can I be needy whilst You have made me rich out of Your magnanimity?\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ لَاْ اِلٰهَ غَيْرُكَ\nWA ANTAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA GHAYROKA \nIt is You, there is no god save You,\nتَعَرَّفْتَ لِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ فَمَا جَهِلَكَ شَيْءٌ\nTA-A’RRAFTA LEKULLE SHAY-IN FAMAA JAHELAKA SHAY-UN \nWho have introduced Yourself to all things; therefore, nothing has ever ignored You.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ تَعَرَّفْتَ اِلَيَّ فِيْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nWA ANTAL LAZEE TA-A’RRAFTA ELAYYA FEE KULLE SHAY-IN \nIt is You Who have introduced Yourself to me in all things;\nفَرَاَيْتُكَ ظَاهِرًا فِيْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nFARA-AYTOKA ZAAHERAN FEE KULLE SHAY-IN \ntherefore, I have seen You Manifest in all things.\nوَاَنْتَ الظَّاهِرُ لِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nWA ANTAZ ZAAHERO LEKULLE SHAY-IN \nIt is You Who give manifestation to all things.\nيَا مَنِ اسْتَوَىٰ بِرَحْمَانِيَّتِهٖ\nYAA MANIS TAWAA BERAHMAANIYYATEHI \nO He Who is firm in power through His All-beneficence;\nفَصَارَ الْعَرْشُ غَيْبًا فِيْ ذَاتِهٖ\nFASAARAL A’RSHO GHAYBAN FEE ZAATEHI \ntherefore, the Throne has become unseen in His Essence.\nمَحَقْتَ الْآثَارَ بِالْآثَارِ\nMAHAQ-TAL AASAARA BIL-AASAARE \nYou have erased the traces by the traces;\nوَمَحَوْتَ الْاَغْيَارَ بِمُحِيْطَاتِ اَفْلَاكِ الْاَنْوَارِ\nWA MAHAW-TAL AGHYAARA BEMOHEETAATE AFLAAKIL ANWAARE \nand You have erased the changeable by the surroundings of the orbits of lights.\nيَا مَنِ احْتَجَبَ فِيْ سُرَادِقَاتِ عَرْشِهٖ\nYAA MANEH TAJABA FEE SORAADEQAATE A’RSHEHI \nO He Who has screened Himself in the curtains of His Throne;\nعَنْ اَنْ تُدْرِكَهُ الْاَبْصَارُ\nA’N AN TUDREKAHUL ABSAARO \nhence, He cannot be comprehended by visions!\nيَا مَنْ تَجَلّٰى بِكَمَالِ بَهَائِهٖ\nYAA MAN TAJALLAA BEKAMAALE BAHAAA-EHI \nO He Who has manifested Himself with His perfect Magnificence;\nفَتَحَقَّقَتْ عَظَمَتُهٗ مِنَ الْاِسْتِوَاءِ\nFATAHAQQAQAT A’ZAMATOHUL ISTEWAAA-E\ntherefore, His Grandeur of being firm in power.\nكَيْفَ تَخْفٰى وَاَنْتَ الظَّاهِرُ؟\nKAYFA TAKHFAA WA ANTAZ ZAAHERO? \nHow can You be hidden whilst You are the Manifester (of all things)?\nاَمْ كَيْفَ تَغِيْبُ \nAM KAYFA TAGHEEBO \nOr how can You be absent whilst You are the Watcher (over all things) \nوَاَنْتَ الرَّقِيْبُ الْحَاضِرُ؟\nWA ANTAR RAQEEBUL HAAZERO? \nand the Present (at all times.)\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nVerily, You have power over all things.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَحْدَهٗ\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE WAHDAHU.\nAll praise be to Allah alone."
}
